<div class="content">

<!-- Hero -->
<div class="hero">
  <h1>RTA-SUM SPM Training Documentation</h1>
  <p>Comprehensive training guide for the Software/Power Manager module &mdash; covering architecture, features, code generation, configuration, testing, and developer workflows.</p>
  <span class="badge">Release 8.1.0</span>
</div>

<!-- Section 1 -->
<h2 id="section-1">1. What is SPM?</h2>

<p><strong>SPM</strong> stands for <strong>Software/Power Manager</strong>. It is an AUTOSAR component developed by ETAS as part of the <strong>RTA-SUM</strong> (Standardized Utility Module) product line for the GM SUM platform. SPM spans two layers: its <strong>Software Manager (SM)</strong> operates at the Application layer alongside other SUM modules, while its <strong>Power Manager (PM)</strong> operates as a CDD with direct hardware access.</p>

<div class="card">
  <h4>In one sentence</h4>
  <p>SPM manages the activation and deactivation of software services and hardware resources across a distributed vehicle network, coordinating power profiles, wakeup sequences, and heartbeat monitoring between ECUs.</p>
</div>

<h3>What SPM does</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Activates/deactivates software services</strong> on local and remote ECUs based on incoming requests</li>
  <li><strong>Manages power profiles</strong> &mdash; each defining a set of software entities and dependencies that must be activated together</li>
  <li><strong>Wakes up remote ECUs</strong> via CAN, Ethernet, TC10, or GPIO when their services are needed</li>
  <li><strong>Monitors remote nodes</strong> via a heartbeat protocol to detect loss-of-communication</li>
  <li><strong>Coordinates shutdown</strong> with the SUSD (Startup/Shutdown) module</li>
  <li><strong>Reports diagnostics</strong> including DID 0xE0DD (profile activation bitmap), DID 0xE0DE/0xE0DF (activity records), and DID 0xE0D7 (activity to SUSD)</li>
  <li><strong>Handles errors</strong> including loss of communication, conflicting requests, low-voltage battery priority, and node faults</li>
</ul>

<h3>What SPM is NOT</h3>
<ul>
  <li>SPM is <strong>not</strong> a Basic Software (BSW) module &mdash; it spans the Application layer (SM) and CDD layer (PM)</li>
  <li>SPM does <strong>not</strong> own the network stack &mdash; it uses RTE ports with SOME/IP transformation for Ethernet frames</li>
  <li>The PM (Power Manager) sub-module operates as a <strong>CDD</strong> with direct hardware access for wakeup and heartbeat; the SM (Software Manager) sub-module sits at the <strong>Application</strong> layer alongside SUSD, SSFM, SSC, and SrvcMgr</li>
</ul>

<h3>Real-World Scenarios</h3>

<details open>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Remote ECU Wakeup for ADAS Feature</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
        <div class="info-box note">
            <div class="box-title">Scenario</div>
            The driver activates the forward collision warning (FCW) feature via the infotainment menu. The FCW profile depends on the ADAS camera ECU, which is currently in sleep mode to conserve battery. SPM must orchestrate the full wakeup and activation sequence.
        </div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 620 519" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="spm_sw1_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- Step 1: Initial state -->
  <rect x="10" y="5" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="11" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#3b82f6"/>
  <text x="29" y="29" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">1</text>
  <text x="52" y="22" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=0ms &#8212; SWC Calls SPM_ActivateProfile</text>
  <text x="52" y="38" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">FCW_AppIntfID validated, enqueued via BFS dispatcher</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="57" x2="310" y2="71" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw1_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 2: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="71" width="600" height="80" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="77" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">2</text>
  <text x="52" y="88" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=5ms &#8212; Dequeue Handler Processes Dependencies</text>
  <text x="52" y="104" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Local FCW profile &#8594; Activating state, SrvcMgr_ActivateServices() called</text>
  <text x="52" y="118" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Remote ADAS_Camera profile &#8594; DevicePowerState = OFF</text>
  <text x="52" y="132" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Triggers PowerOnDevice()</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="151" x2="310" y2="165" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw1_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 3: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="165" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="171" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="189" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">3</text>
  <text x="52" y="182" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=10ms &#8212; PGTT Wakeup Step 1</text>
  <text x="52" y="198" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">EthSM_RequestComMode() sends TC10 wakeup pulse</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="217" x2="310" y2="231" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw1_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 4: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="231" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="237" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="255" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">4</text>
  <text x="52" y="248" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=60ms &#8212; PGTT Wakeup Step 2 (SpmSeqStepDly=50ms)</text>
  <text x="52" y="264" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Ethernet WUF-A sent to camera IP</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="283" x2="310" y2="297" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw1_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 5: Detection / success -->
  <rect x="10" y="297" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="303" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f59e0b"/>
  <text x="29" y="321" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">5</text>
  <text x="52" y="314" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">T=1200ms &#8212; Heartbeat Detected</text>
  <text x="52" y="330" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Camera ECU heartbeat counter incrementing &#8594; DevicePowerState = ON</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="349" x2="310" y2="363" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw1_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 6: Notification -->
  <rect x="10" y="363" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#fff8e6" stroke="#f39c12" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="369" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f39c12"/>
  <text x="29" y="387" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">6</text>
  <text x="52" y="380" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#b45309">T=1210ms &#8212; SM Sends ACTIVATE Command</text>
  <text x="52" y="396" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">SM Frame sent to camera ECU for ADAS_Camera profile</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="415" x2="310" y2="429" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw1_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 7: Success -->
  <rect x="10" y="429" width="600" height="40" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="435" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="453" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">7</text>
  <text x="52" y="452" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=1260ms &#8212; Camera ECU Acknowledges Activation</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="469" x2="310" y2="483" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw1_arr)"/>
  <!-- KEY POINT -->
  <rect x="10" y="483" width="600" height="36" rx="8" fill="#f3e8ff" stroke="#a855f7" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="310" y="506" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">&#9733; Wakeup is step-based (PGTT); SM waits for heartbeat before sending activation SM Frame</text>
</svg>
    </div>
</details>

<details open>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Heartbeat Loss Detection</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
        <div class="info-box note">
            <div class="box-title">Scenario</div>
            A remote ECU hosting the parking assist profile experiences a software fault and stops sending heartbeats. SPM must detect the loss, report it for diagnostics, and deactivate dependent profiles.
        </div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 620 453" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="spm_sw2_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- Step 1: Initial state -->
  <rect x="10" y="5" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="11" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#3b82f6"/>
  <text x="29" y="29" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">1</text>
  <text x="52" y="22" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=0ms &#8212; Initial State</text>
  <text x="52" y="38" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Remote ECU heartbeat counter = 0x00001234, DevicePowerState = ON</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="57" x2="310" y2="71" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw2_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 2: Detection -->
  <rect x="10" y="71" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="77" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f59e0b"/>
  <text x="29" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">2</text>
  <text x="52" y="88" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">T=100ms &#8212; Heartbeat Monitor Cycle 1</text>
  <text x="52" y="104" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Counter unchanged (still 0x00001234), noHbCnt incremented</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="123" x2="310" y2="137" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw2_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 3: Detection -->
  <rect x="10" y="137" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="143" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f59e0b"/>
  <text x="29" y="161" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">3</text>
  <text x="52" y="154" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">T=200ms &#8212; Heartbeat Monitor Cycle 2</text>
  <text x="52" y="170" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Counter still 0x00001234, noHbCnt incremented again</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="189" x2="310" y2="203" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw2_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 4: Error / fault -->
  <rect x="10" y="203" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#ffeef0" stroke="#e74c3c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="209" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#e74c3c"/>
  <text x="29" y="227" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">4</text>
  <text x="52" y="220" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#c0392b">T=300ms &#8212; Heartbeat Monitor Cycle 3 &#8212; Threshold Reached</text>
  <text x="52" y="236" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Counter still 0x00001234, noHbCnt reaches threshold</text>
  <text x="52" y="250" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">DevicePowerState transitions ON &#8594; Faulted</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="269" x2="310" y2="283" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw2_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 5: Notification -->
  <rect x="10" y="283" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#fff8e6" stroke="#f39c12" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="289" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f39c12"/>
  <text x="29" y="307" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">5</text>
  <text x="52" y="300" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#b45309">T=305ms &#8212; DTC Reported to SSFM</text>
  <text x="52" y="316" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Sum_Spm_WriteLossofNode() sends DTC base ID to SSFM for diagnostic reporting</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="335" x2="310" y2="349" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw2_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 6: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="349" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="355" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="373" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">6</text>
  <text x="52" y="366" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=310ms &#8212; Requester Cleanup and Stay-Awake</text>
  <text x="52" y="382" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Spm_LoC_wRequester_Handler() sends REJECTED_LOSS_OF_HEARTBEAT feedback</text>
  <text x="52" y="396" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Removes requester from profile lists, starts SpmStayAwakeTimer</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="415" x2="310" y2="429" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw2_arr)"/>
  <!-- KEY POINT -->
  <rect x="10" y="429" width="600" height="24" rx="8" fill="#f3e8ff" stroke="#a855f7" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="310" y="446" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">&#9733; Three consecutive missed heartbeats trigger Faulted state; SSFM notified for DTC logging</text>
</svg>
    </div>
</details>

<details open>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Low Voltage Battery Priority</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
        <div class="info-box note">
            <div class="box-title">Scenario</div>
            During a cold winter start, battery voltage drops below threshold. The Vehicle Energy Optimizer raises the priority threshold, and SPM must shed non-critical profiles while keeping safety-critical ones active.
        </div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 620 545" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="spm_sw3_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- Step 1: Initial state -->
  <rect x="10" y="5" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="11" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#3b82f6"/>
  <text x="29" y="29" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">1</text>
  <text x="52" y="22" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=0s &#8212; Vehicle Cranking, Low Voltage</text>
  <text x="52" y="38" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Battery voltage = 11.2V &#8594; VEO raises priority threshold to HIGH</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="57" x2="310" y2="71" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw3_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 2: Notification -->
  <rect x="10" y="71" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#fff8e6" stroke="#f39c12" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="77" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f39c12"/>
  <text x="29" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">2</text>
  <text x="52" y="88" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#b45309">T=0.1s &#8212; SSFM Forwards Priority Level</text>
  <text x="52" y="104" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">New priority level forwarded to SPM via RTE port</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="123" x2="310" y2="137" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw3_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 3: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="137" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="143" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="161" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">3</text>
  <text x="52" y="154" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=0.15s &#8212; Profile Evaluation Begins</text>
  <text x="52" y="170" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Spm_ErrorHandler_LowVoltageBattery() runs periodic check on all active profiles</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="189" x2="310" y2="203" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw3_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 4: Error / shedding -->
  <rect x="10" y="203" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#ffeef0" stroke="#e74c3c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="209" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#e74c3c"/>
  <text x="29" y="227" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">4</text>
  <text x="52" y="220" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#c0392b">T=0.15s &#8212; Non-Critical Profiles Shed</text>
  <text x="52" y="236" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Seat_Heater (LOW) &#8594; REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER, deactivated</text>
  <text x="52" y="250" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Ambient_Lighting (MEDIUM) &#8594; REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER, deactivated</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="269" x2="310" y2="283" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw3_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 5: Success / retention -->
  <rect x="10" y="283" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="289" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="307" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">5</text>
  <text x="52" y="300" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=0.15s &#8212; Safety-Critical Profiles Retained</text>
  <text x="52" y="316" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">EPS_Steering (CRITICAL &gt; HIGH) &#8594; remains active</text>
  <text x="52" y="330" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">ESC_Braking (CRITICAL &gt; HIGH) &#8594; remains active</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="349" x2="310" y2="363" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw3_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 6: Recovery -->
  <rect x="10" y="363" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="369" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="387" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">6</text>
  <text x="52" y="380" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=5.0s &#8212; Battery Voltage Recovers</text>
  <text x="52" y="396" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Voltage recovers to 12.8V &#8594; VEO lowers threshold back to LOW</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="415" x2="310" y2="429" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw3_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 7: Success -->
  <rect x="10" y="429" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="435" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="453" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">7</text>
  <text x="52" y="446" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=5.1s &#8212; Activations Allowed Again</text>
  <text x="52" y="462" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">SWCs may re-request shed profiles; SPM allows activation again</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="481" x2="310" y2="495" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw3_arr)"/>
  <!-- KEY POINT -->
  <rect x="10" y="495" width="600" height="50" rx="8" fill="#f3e8ff" stroke="#a855f7" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="310" y="514" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">&#9733; Safety-critical profiles (CRITICAL) are never shed. Comfort features are shed first</text>
  <text x="310" y="530" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">and can be re-activated once voltage recovers.</text>
</svg>
    </div>
</details>

<details open>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Coordinated Multi-ECU Shutdown</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
        <div class="info-box note">
            <div class="box-title">Scenario</div>
            The driver turns off the vehicle. SUSD initiates a coordinated shutdown. SPM must deactivate all profiles on remote ECUs, wait for acknowledgments, send final heartbeats, and then report shutdown readiness.
        </div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 620 531" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="spm_sw4_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- Step 1: Initial / trigger -->
  <rect x="10" y="5" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="11" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#3b82f6"/>
  <text x="29" y="29" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">1</text>
  <text x="52" y="22" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=0s &#8212; Driver Key-Off</text>
  <text x="52" y="38" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">SUSD deasserts PermitExecution bit 0 (Wakeups Active)</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="57" x2="310" y2="71" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw4_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 2: Detection -->
  <rect x="10" y="71" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="77" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f59e0b"/>
  <text x="29" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">2</text>
  <text x="52" y="88" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">T=0.05s &#8212; SPM Detects Shutdown</text>
  <text x="52" y="104" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Transitions to Spm_PrepareToShutdown</text>
  <text x="52" y="118" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Spm_ErrorHandler_ShutdownDetected() called, request queue flushed</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="137" x2="310" y2="151" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw4_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 3: Notification -->
  <rect x="10" y="151" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#fff8e6" stroke="#f39c12" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="157" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f39c12"/>
  <text x="29" y="175" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">3</text>
  <text x="52" y="168" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#b45309">T=0.1s &#8212; DEACTIVATE SM Frames Sent</text>
  <text x="52" y="184" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">SPM sends DEACTIVATE to all remote ECUs with active profiles</text>
  <text x="52" y="198" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">(Camera ECU, Radar ECU, Body Controller)</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="217" x2="310" y2="231" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw4_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 4: Success -->
  <rect x="10" y="231" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="237" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="255" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">4</text>
  <text x="52" y="248" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=0.5s &#8212; Camera and Radar Acknowledge</text>
  <text x="52" y="264" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Camera ECU acknowledges deactivation; Radar ECU acknowledges</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="283" x2="310" y2="297" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw4_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 5: Success -->
  <rect x="10" y="297" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="303" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="321" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">5</text>
  <text x="52" y="314" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=0.8s &#8212; Body Controller Acknowledges</text>
  <text x="52" y="330" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">All remote profiles now Inactive</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="349" x2="310" y2="363" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw4_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 6: Notification -->
  <rect x="10" y="363" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#fff8e6" stroke="#f39c12" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="369" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f39c12"/>
  <text x="29" y="387" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">6</text>
  <text x="52" y="380" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#b45309">T=1.0s &#8212; Final Heartbeat Sent</text>
  <text x="52" y="396" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Sum_Spm_CheckHBCounterShallBeSentFullScale() sends final full-scale heartbeat</text>
  <text x="52" y="410" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">ShutdownPermission set to 0xFF (vote for shutdown)</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="429" x2="310" y2="443" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw4_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 7: Success -->
  <rect x="10" y="443" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="449" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="467" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">7</text>
  <text x="52" y="460" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=1.2s &#8212; Shutdown Ready</text>
  <text x="52" y="476" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">ShutdownPermission set to 0xFE &#8594; SUSD proceeds with ECU power-down</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="495" x2="310" y2="509" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw4_arr)"/>
  <!-- KEY POINT -->
  <rect x="10" y="509" width="600" height="22" rx="8" fill="#f3e8ff" stroke="#a855f7" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="310" y="525" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">&#9733; Two-phase shutdown: 0xFF signals intent, 0xFE signals completion. SUSD waits for all 0xFE.</text>
</svg>
    </div>
</details>

<hr>

<!-- Section 2 -->
<h2 id="section-2">2. Why does SPM exist?</h2>

<h3>The Problem</h3>
<p>Modern vehicles (SDV &mdash; Software Defined Vehicles) contain dozens of ECUs across multiple domains (powertrain, body, infotainment, ADAS). These ECUs host software services that depend on each other. When a feature is requested:</p>

<ol>
  <li>The ECU hosting the service might be <strong>powered off</strong> &mdash; it needs to be woken up</li>
  <li>The service might depend on <strong>other services on other ECUs</strong> &mdash; a chain of activations</li>
  <li>The requesting ECU needs to know when the service is <strong>ready</strong> or if it <strong>failed</strong></li>
  <li>When services are no longer needed, ECUs should <strong>shut down</strong> to save battery</li>
</ol>

<h3>The Solution: SPM</h3>
<p>SPM provides a <strong>standardized, configurable framework</strong> for:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Problem</th><th>SPM Solution</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>"How do I know which services to activate?"</td><td><strong>Power Profiles</strong> &mdash; preconfigured bundles of services and dependencies</td></tr>
    <tr><td>"How do I wake up a sleeping ECU?"</td><td><strong>Power Graph Traversal Table (PGTT)</strong> &mdash; wakeup sequences using TC10, CAN WUF, ETH WUF, GPIO</td></tr>
    <tr><td>"How do I know if a remote ECU is alive?"</td><td><strong>Heartbeat monitoring</strong> &mdash; rolling counter broadcast on multicast Ethernet</td></tr>
    <tr><td>"How do I request a service on another ECU?"</td><td><strong>SM Frame protocol</strong> &mdash; SOME/IP frames carrying activation/status messages between SPM instances</td></tr>
    <tr><td>"How do I coordinate shutdown?"</td><td><strong>SUSD interaction</strong> &mdash; PermitExecution/ShutdownPermission handshake</td></tr>
    <tr><td>"How do I handle errors?"</td><td><strong>Error handling</strong> &mdash; loss-of-com detection, retry policies, DTC reporting to SSFM</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Specifications</h3>
<p>SPM implements requirements from GM specifications:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>SDV-2017</strong> &mdash; Vehicle Power Management Architecture</li>
  <li><strong>SDV-8217</strong> &mdash; Mechatronic Power Manager Infrastructure Specification</li>
  <li><strong>SDV-8201</strong> &mdash; Service Discovery Extension Specification</li>
  <li><strong>SDV-6001</strong> &mdash; Diagnostic Infrastructure Specification</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<!-- Section 3 -->
<h2 id="section-3">3. System Architecture Overview</h2>

<h3>Network Topology</h3>
<p>SPM operates in a <strong>distributed graph-based network</strong> where:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Edge Nodes</strong> &mdash; ECUs at the periphery of the network (e.g., sensors, actuators)</li>
  <li><strong>Intermediate Nodes</strong> &mdash; ECUs that act as gateways (e.g., CHM &mdash; Central Hub Module) connecting edge nodes</li>
</ul>

<div class="net-topo">
  <div class="net-row"><div class="net-node">Edge ECU A<br><small style="font-weight:400;font-size:11px">12.10.2.2</small></div></div>
  <div class="net-link-v"></div>
  <div class="net-link-label">Ethernet</div>
  <div class="net-link-v"></div>
  <div class="net-row">
    <div class="net-node">Edge ECU B<br><small style="font-weight:400;font-size:11px">12.10.2.3</small></div>
    <div class="net-link-h"></div>
    <div class="net-node hub">CHM / Intermediate<br><small style="font-weight:400;font-size:11px;opacity:.8">12.10.2.1 (this ECU)</small></div>
    <div class="net-link-h"></div>
    <div class="net-node">Edge ECU C<br><small style="font-weight:400;font-size:11px">12.10.2.4</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="net-link-v"></div>
  <div class="net-link-label">CAN</div>
  <div class="net-link-v"></div>
  <div class="net-row"><div class="net-node">Edge ECU D<br><small style="font-weight:400;font-size:11px">12.10.3.1</small></div></div>
</div>

<p>Each ECU runs its own SPM instance. SPM instances communicate with each other using:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>SM Frames</strong> (Software Manager frames) over Ethernet/SOME/IP for activation/deactivation requests and status</li>
  <li><strong>PM Frames</strong> (Power Manager frames) over Ethernet/SOME/IP for heartbeat</li>
  <li><strong>Wake-Up Frames</strong> over CAN and/or Ethernet for selective wake-up of sleeping ECUs</li>
</ul>

<h3>Two Sub-Modules</h3>
<p>SPM is split across two AUTOSAR layers. The two sub-modules share the same codebase but run at different architectural levels:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Sub-Module</th><th>AUTOSAR Layer</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Periodic Runnable</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Software Manager (SM)</strong></td>
      <td style="color:#6c5ce7;font-weight:600;">Application</td>
      <td>Service activation/deactivation, request handling, requester list management, SM frame exchange</td>
      <td><code>RE_SPM_SoftMgr_MainFunction</code> (configurable period)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Power Manager (PM)</strong></td>
      <td style="color:#e8913a;font-weight:600;">CDD</td>
      <td>Heartbeat Tx/Rx, wakeup sequence execution, device power state tracking, wake-up frame handling (direct HW access)</td>
      <td><code>RE_SPM_PowerManager_MainFunction</code> (fixed 5ms period)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>SPM in the AUTOSAR Stack</h3>

<svg class="arch-interactive" viewBox="0 0 900 480" style="max-width:900px;width:100%;height:auto;margin:16px auto 24px;display:block;font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;">
<defs>
  <marker id="spm_arr1" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,3 L0,6" fill="#94a3b8"/></marker>
  <marker id="spm_arr1b" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="0" refY="3" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M8,0 L0,3 L8,6" fill="#94a3b8"/></marker>
  <filter id="spm_sh1"><feDropShadow dx="0" dy="2" stdDeviation="3" flood-opacity="0.08"/></filter>
</defs>

<!-- ===== AUTOSAR Layer Bands ===== -->
<!-- Application Layer -->
<rect x="5" y="5" width="890" height="110" rx="8" fill="#eff6ff" stroke="#bfdbfe" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="20" y="26" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af" opacity="0.6">Application Layer</text>

<!-- RTE -->
<rect x="5" y="125" width="890" height="30" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#fbbf24" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="450" y="145" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">RTE (Runtime Environment)</text>

<!-- BSW Services Layer -->
<rect x="5" y="168" width="890" height="108" rx="8" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#86efac" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="20" y="190" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534" opacity="0.6">BSW Services Layer</text>

<!-- CDD Layer -->
<rect x="5" y="290" width="890" height="95" rx="8" fill="#fef2f2" stroke="#fca5a5" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="20" y="312" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#991b1b" opacity="0.6">Complex Device Driver (CDD)</text>

<!-- MCAL / Hardware -->
<rect x="5" y="400" width="890" height="65" rx="8" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<text x="20" y="425" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#475569" opacity="0.6">MCAL / Hardware</text>

<!-- ===== Application Layer Blocks ===== -->
<g class="module-box" data-module="SUSD">
  <rect x="130" y="25" width="100" height="62" rx="6" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5" filter="url(#spm_sh1)"/>
  <text x="180" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">SUSD</text>
  <text x="180" y="63" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#92400e">Startup / Shutdown</text>
