<hr>

<!-- Section 4 -->
<h2 id="section-4">4. Core Concepts</h2>

<h3 id="section-4-1">4.1 Power Profiles</h3>

<p>A <strong>Power Profile</strong> (also called Activation Profile) is the central concept in SPM. It represents a configurable bundle containing:</p>
<ul>
  <li>A <strong>Service ID + Instance ID</strong> (4 bytes: 2 bytes service, 2 bytes instance)</li>
  <li>A <strong>Profile Number</strong> (1 byte)</li>
  <li>An <strong>Application Interface ID</strong> (used by local SWCs to request activation)</li>
  <li><strong>Dependencies</strong> &mdash; other Power Profiles that must also be activated</li>
  <li><strong>PDU Group associations</strong> &mdash; communication groups to enable/disable</li>
  <li><strong>Low Voltage Priority levels</strong> (Vehicle ON / Vehicle OFF)</li>
  <li><strong>Activation timeout</strong> for Vehicle OFF mode</li>
</ul>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Example</h4>
  <p>A navigation service profile might depend on:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A map rendering service (local dependency)</li>
    <li>A GPS data service (remote dependency on another ECU)</li>
    <li>A network communication PDU group (consumed dependency)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h4>Dependency Types</h4>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Type</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SUM_PRF_DEP_ACT_AND_CONS</code></td><td>Activate the service AND enable its PDU group</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SUM_PRF_ACITVATED</code></td><td>Activate the service only</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SUM_PRF_CONSUMED</code></td><td>Enable the PDU group only (don't activate the service)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>Local vs Remote Profiles</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Local Profile</strong>: The service runs on the same ECU. SPM activates it by calling <code>SrvcMgr_ActivateServices()</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Remote Profile</strong>: The service runs on another ECU. SPM sends an activation request via SM Frame to the remote SPM.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="section-4-2">4.2 Power Graph Traversal Table (PGTT)</h3>

<p>The PGTT defines the <strong>network topology and wakeup sequences</strong> from the perspective of one SPM instance:</p>

<pre><code>PGTT
 +-- SpmWkngDvc (Waking Device = this ECU)
 |    +-- SpmNodeType (Edge or Intermediate)
 |    +-- SpmSrcIp / SpmDstIp (HB source/destination per VLAN)
 |    +-- SpmVLANId (VLAN identifiers)
 |    +-- SpmIntermediateDstAddrs (ETH WUF destination IPs)
 |    +-- SpmTrgDvcInfo (links targets to wakeup sequences)
 |         +-- SpmTrgDvcRef --&gt; SpmTrgDvc
 |         +-- SpmWkUpSeqRef --&gt; SpmWkUpSeq
 |
 +-- SpmTrgDvc[] (Target Devices = remote ECUs)
 |    +-- SpmTrgDvcID (IP addresses)
 |    +-- SpmTrgDvcDtcBaseID (DTC code for Loss-of-Node)
 |    +-- SpmTrgDvcTimeOut (heartbeat timeout)
 |    +-- SpmTrgDvcHndlngInfo (for intermediate nodes: WUF mapping)
 |
 +-- SpmWkUpSeq[] (Wakeup Sequences)
      +-- SpmWkUpSteq[] (Wakeup Steps, ordered)
           +-- SpmSeqStepID (order)
           +-- SpmSeqStepDly (delay before next step, ms)
           +-- SpmCommandType (TC10, ETH WUF, CAN WUF, GPIO)
           +-- SpmCommandValue (port number or bit position)</code></pre>

<h3 id="section-4-3">4.3 Heartbeat Protocol</h3>

<p>Every SPM instance broadcasts a <strong>heartbeat</strong> (PM frame) on multicast Ethernet to signal its availability:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Field</th><th>Size</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Custom Header (SrcPM_ID)</td><td>4 bytes</td><td>Source IP address</td></tr>
    <tr><td>HeartbeatCounter</td><td>4 bytes (uint32)</td><td>Rolling counter: 0, 1, 2, ...</td></tr>
    <tr><td>NumberProfileActive</td><td>2 bytes (uint16)</td><td>Number of non-INACTIVE profiles</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p><strong>Key behaviors:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>First HB value is <strong>0</strong>, increments by 1 each transmission</li>
  <li><strong>Burst phase</strong>: first 3 counts sent at 5ms (calibratable)</li>
  <li><strong>Steady state</strong>: subsequent counts at 1s (calibratable)</li>
  <li><strong>Shutdown indication</strong>: counter &ge; <code>0xFFFFFF00</code> means shutdown pending</li>
  <li><strong>Full-scale counter</strong> (<code>0xFFFFFFFF</code>): sent when SUSD deasserts PermitExecution</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>How heartbeat is used to detect device state:</strong></p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Observed HB Behavior</th><th>Interpreted State</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Normal HB received (not in shutdown range) from Off/Initializing</td><td><strong>On</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><td>HB counter decreases (reboot detected)</td><td><strong>Reboot</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><td>HB &ge; 0xFFFFFF00</td><td><strong>Pending Shutdown</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><td>No HB received within DTC timeout</td><td><strong>Faulted</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Device no longer monitored (not Requested/Requester) + timeout</td><td><strong>Off</strong></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: HB Transmission &mdash; Burst &amp; Steady State</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_HeartBeat_Mgr.h</code> &mdash; key constants and data structure:</p>
<pre><code>#define SPM_NUMBER_OF_INITIALSENDING   (0x03u)   // 3 burst transmissions
#define SPM_INITIAL_DEBOUNCE_DELAY_HB_TICK  (SPM_INITIAL_DEBOUNCE_DELAY_HB_MS / SUM_SPM_PERIOD_PM_MAINFUNCTION_MS)  // ~5ms
#define SPM_STEADYSTATE_DELAY_HB_TICK       (SPM_STEADYSTATE_DELAY_HB_MS / SUM_SPM_PERIOD_PM_MAINFUNCTION_MS)       // ~1000ms

typedef struct {
    SPM_HB_dt_Prv  Spm_PayloadToWrite;      // { SrcPMId, HrtBtCntr, NmbrPrfAct }
    uint8          Spm_InitialBurstPhase;    // counts 0..2 during burst
    uint16         Spm_TimerTracker_Tick;    // countdown timer in ticks
} Spm_HB_Tx_InfoType;</code></pre>

  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_HeartBeat_Mgr.c</code> &mdash; the timer handler called every PM main cycle:</p>
<pre><code>static void Spm_HandlerHBTxTimer(void) {
    (Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_TimerTracker_Tick)--;

    // Send when timer expires OR during shutdown (only once)
    if ((Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_TimerTracker_Tick == 0x00u) ||
        (Sum_Spm_GetHBCounterShallBeSentFullScale() &amp;&amp; !Sum_Spm_IsFinalHeartbeatSent()))
    {
        // Populate active profile count
        Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_PayloadToWrite.NmbrPrfAct = Spm_GetNotInactiveLocalProfNumberForHB();

        // Send on each configured network
        for (i = 0U; i &lt; SUM_SPM_NUMBER_OF_NET_CONF; i++) {
            Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_PayloadToWrite.SrcPMId = SPM_GET_HB_SRCIP(i);
            (void)SPM_Send_PMFrame(&amp;Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_PayloadToWrite);
        }

        (Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_PayloadToWrite.HrtBtCntr)++;  // increment counter

        // Burst vs Steady state switch
        if (Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_InitialBurstPhase &lt; (SPM_NUMBER_OF_INITIALSENDING - 1u)) {
            Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_InitialBurstPhase++;
            Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_TimerTracker_Tick = SPM_INITIAL_DEBOUNCE_DELAY_HB_TICK;  // fast 5ms
        } else {
            Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_TimerTracker_Tick = SPM_STEADYSTATE_DELAY_HB_TICK;       // slow 1s
        }

        // Latch final HB after shutdown send
        if (Sum_Spm_GetHBCounterShallBeSentFullScale()) {
            Sum_Spm_Set_FinalHeartbeatSent(TRUE);
        }
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>The outer handler checks if full-scale HB is needed (shutdown) before calling the timer:</p>
<pre><code>void Spm_PM_HB_Tx_Handler(void) {
    if (TRUE == Sum_Spm_GetHBCounterShallBeSentFullScale()) {
        Spm_HB_Tx_Info.Spm_PayloadToWrite.HrtBtCntr = SPM_HB_CNTR_MAX_VALUE;  // 0xFFFFFFFF
    }
    if (RTE_MODE_MDG_SPM_CommunicationReady_SPM_COM_READY == Rte_Mode_RP_SPM_BswM_CommunicationReady_SPM_MDG_CR()) {
        Spm_HandlerHBTxTimer();
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p><strong>HB Reception</strong> &mdash; penultimate/previous tracking for reboot detection:</p>
<pre><code>void Spm_PM_Rx_Polling_Handler(void) {
    while (E_OK == Spm_HandleVLANCommunication(..., SPM_HB_COMHNDLING, &amp;Sum_Spm_HB_data, ...)) {
        Sum_Spm_IndexOfSrcId = Spm_GetIndexTrgDvcFromIP(Sum_Spm_HB_data.SrcPMId);
        if (Sum_Spm_IndexOfSrcId != SPM_INVALID) {
            Sum_Spm_SetStateHBRemote(idx, TRUE);                       // mark HB received
            Sum_Spm_SetPenultimateHBval(idx, Sum_Spm_GetPreviousHBval(idx));  // shift history
            Sum_Spm_SetPreviousHBval(idx, Sum_Spm_HB_data.HrtBtCntr);        // store current
        }
    }
}
// Reboot detection: if PreviousHBval &lt; PenultimateHBval =&gt; counter decreased =&gt; reboot!</code></pre>
</div>

<h3 id="section-4-4">4.4 SM Frame Protocol</h3>

<p>The SM (Software Manager) frame carries activation/deactivation messages between SPM instances:</p>

<div style="margin:16px 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0;">
  <!-- Header -->
  <div style="display:flex;gap:0;">
    <div style="background:#636e72;color:white;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;flex:1;border-radius:8px 0 0 0;">PMSrcId<br><small style="opacity:.7">4 bytes &mdash; Source IP</small></div>
    <div style="background:#636e72;color:white;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;flex:1;border-radius:0 8px 0 0;">PMDestId<br><small style="opacity:.7">4 bytes &mdash; Destination IP</small></div>
  </div>
  <!-- PROFILE_REQUEST -->
  <div style="background:#0984e3;color:white;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">
    MsgType = 0x00: PROFILE_REQUEST
  </div>
  <div style="display:flex;gap:0;">
    <div style="background:#74b9ff;padding:8px 12px;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;flex:1;border-right:1px solid white;">Size Indicator<br><small>2 bytes</small></div>
    <div style="background:#a4d4ff;padding:8px 12px;font-size:11px;flex:2;">
      <strong>Entry[] &times; N:</strong> ProfileID_SWID <span style="color:#636e72">(4B)</span> + ProfileNumber <span style="color:#636e72">(1B)</span> + RequestType <span style="color:#636e72">(1B)</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <!-- REQ_STATUS_PROF_STATE -->
  <div style="background:#e8913a;color:white;padding:10px 14px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;">
    MsgType = 0x01: REQ_STATUS_PROF_STATE
  </div>
  <div style="display:flex;gap:0;">
    <div style="background:#ffeaa7;padding:8px 12px;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;flex:1;border-right:1px solid white;border-radius:0 0 0 8px;">Size Indicator<br><small>2 bytes</small></div>
    <div style="background:#fff3cd;padding:8px 12px;font-size:11px;flex:2;border-radius:0 0 8px 0;">
      <strong>Entry[] &times; N:</strong> ProfileID_SWID <span style="color:#636e72">(4B)</span> + ProfileNumber <span style="color:#636e72">(1B)</span> + ReqStatus <span style="color:#636e72">(1B)</span> + ProfileState <span style="color:#636e72">(1B)</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p><strong>Request enumerations:</strong> EMPTY (0x00), ACTIVATE (0x01), DEACTIVATE (0x02)</p>
<p><strong>Request status values:</strong> OK_ACTIVATION (0x01), OK_DEACTIVATION (0x02), various REJECTED codes</p>
<p><strong>Profile states:</strong> INACTIVE (0x00), ACTIVATING (0x01), ACTIVATED (0x02), DEACTIVATING (0x03), UNKNOWN (0xFF)</p>

<blockquote>
  <p><strong>Implementation note:</strong> Internally, the generated code uses a richer enum <code>SpmPowPrfStatusEnumType</code> with additional states: <code>Inactive</code>, <code>Activating</code>, <code>ActivationFailed</code>, <code>Activated</code>, <code>ImmDeactivation</code>, <code>Deactivating</code>. The SM Frame protocol maps these to the simpler set above.</p>
</blockquote>

<p><strong>Rejection codes (16 defined):</strong> <code>Spm_REJECTED_PROFILE_UNKNOWN</code>, <code>Spm_REJECTED_LACK_OF_PERMISSION</code>, <code>Spm_REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER</code>, <code>Spm_REJECTED_THERMAL_CAPABILITY</code>, <code>Spm_REJECTED_PROFILE_BLOCKED</code>, <code>Spm_REJECTED_LOSS_OF_HEARTBEAT</code>, <code>Spm_REJECTED_RESET_DETECTED</code>, <code>Spm_REJECTED_REQUEST_INVALID</code>, among others. These drive tiered retry behavior (fast vs slow periodicity) in the profile FSM.</p>

<h3 id="section-4-5">4.5 Device Power States</h3>

<p>SPM tracks the power state of each target device through a state machine:</p>

<div class="svg-wrap">
<svg viewBox="0 0 700 380" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:Segoe UI,sans-serif;max-width:700px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="ah" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#1a3a5c"/></marker>
    <marker id="ah-r" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#d63031"/></marker>
    <marker id="ah-g" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#00b894"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- States -->
  <rect x="20" y="150" width="100" height="50" rx="25" fill="#f8f9fa" stroke="#636e72" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <text x="70" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="13" fill="#636e72">Off</text>

  <rect x="180" y="40" width="130" height="50" rx="25" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#0984e3" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <text x="245" y="70" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="13" fill="#0984e3">Initializing</text>

  <rect x="370" y="150" width="100" height="50" rx="25" fill="#e6fff7" stroke="#00b894" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <text x="420" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="13" fill="#00b894">On</text>

  <rect x="570" y="150" width="100" height="50" rx="25" fill="#fff0f0" stroke="#d63031" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <text x="620" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="13" fill="#d63031">Faulted</text>

  <rect x="370" y="300" width="130" height="50" rx="25" fill="#fffbea" stroke="#fdcb6e" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <text x="435" y="325" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="12" fill="#e17055">Pending Shutdown</text>

  <rect x="570" y="300" width="100" height="50" rx="25" fill="#fff8f0" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2.5"/>
  <text x="620" y="330" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="13" fill="#e8913a">Reboot</text>

  <!-- Off -> Initializing -->
  <line x1="100" y1="150" x2="190" y2="90" stroke="#1a3a5c" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
  <text x="120" y="110" font-size="10" fill="#1a3a5c" font-weight="600">Requested/Requester</text>

  <!-- Initializing -> On -->
  <line x1="310" y1="85" x2="390" y2="150" stroke="#00b894" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah-g)"/>
  <text x="370" y="110" font-size="10" fill="#00b894" font-weight="600">HB received</text>

  <!-- Initializing -> Faulted -->
  <line x1="310" y1="55" x2="575" y2="160" stroke="#d63031" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah-r)"/>
  <text x="440" y="90" font-size="10" fill="#d63031" font-weight="600">timeout (still monitored)</text>

  <!-- On -> Faulted -->
  <line x1="470" y1="165" x2="570" y2="168" stroke="#d63031" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah-r)"/>
  <text x="510" y="158" font-size="10" fill="#d63031" font-weight="600">No HB timeout</text>

  <!-- On -> PendingShutdown -->
  <line x1="420" y1="200" x2="430" y2="300" stroke="#e17055" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
  <text x="445" y="255" font-size="10" fill="#e17055" font-weight="600">HB &ge; 0xFFFFFF00</text>

  <!-- Faulted -> Reboot -->
  <line x1="620" y1="200" x2="620" y2="300" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
  <text x="635" y="255" font-size="10" fill="#e8913a" font-weight="600">HB counter dec</text>

  <!-- Reboot -> On -->
  <path d="M570,320 Q520,290 470,195" fill="none" stroke="#00b894" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah-g)"/>
  <text x="500" y="275" font-size="10" fill="#00b894" font-weight="600">HB increase</text>

  <!-- PendingShutdown / Off (back) -->
  <path d="M370,335 Q200,360 70,200" fill="none" stroke="#636e72" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,3" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
  <text x="170" y="330" font-size="10" fill="#636e72">timeout, not monitored</text>
</svg>
</div>

<p>Each target device can be tagged as:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Requested</strong>: SPM has requested activation of a remote profile hosted on this device</li>
  <li><strong>Requester</strong>: This device has requested activation of a profile on our ECU</li>
  <li>Both simultaneously</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<!-- Section 5 -->
<h2 id="section-5">5. Feature Deep-Dives</h2>

<h3 id="section-5-1">5.1 Profile Activation Flow</h3>

<p>When a local SWC calls <code>SPM_ActivateProfile(ApplicationInterfaceID)</code>:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Validation</strong>: SPM checks the ApplicationInterfaceID is known, <code>SpmLocActivationAllowed</code> is true, no conflicting deactivation is in progress, learning session is not pending</li>
  <li><strong>Low Voltage Priority Check</strong>: If configured, checks battery priority level allows activation</li>
  <li><strong>Vehicle Power Mode Check</strong>: If Vehicle OFF, checks <code>SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff</code> &gt; 0</li>
  <li><strong>DID E0DE/E0DF Update</strong>: Updates diagnostic activity records (if in PowerOff session)</li>
  <li><strong>Request Dispatching</strong>: <code>Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher()</code> enqueues the profile AND all its dependencies recursively</li>
  <li><strong>Requester List Population</strong>: Dequeue handler processes items and calls <code>Spm_RequesterList_ActivationRequestHandler()</code> to add the requester (IP=0 for local) to each profile's requester list</li>
  <li><strong>FSM Processing</strong>: <code>Spm_LocalPowerProfile_FSM()</code> (periodic) detects the new requester:
    <ul>
      <li>If profile is Inactive &rarr; transitions to <strong>Activating</strong></li>
      <li>Calls <code>SrvcMgr_ActivateServices()</code> to activate the service</li>
      <li>If successful &rarr; transitions to <strong>Activated</strong></li>
      <li>Enables PDU groups via BswM mode switch</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Remote Dependencies</strong>: For each remote dependency, <code>Spm_RemotePowerProfile_FSM()</code>:
    <ul>
      <li>Checks DevicePowerState of the target ECU</li>
      <li>If OFF &rarr; triggers <code>PowerOnDevice()</code> wakeup sequence</li>
      <li>If ON &rarr; sends ACTIVATE command via SM Frame</li>
      <li>Periodically retries until acknowledged</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<details>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Rear Camera Profile Activation with Dependency Resolution</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
