<details>
    <summary>Implementation Example &mdash; Sum_Spm_ActivateProfile (from Sum_Spm_Services.c)</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
<pre><span class="cm">/* Profile activation API entry point - validates request and dispatches to BFS */</span>
<span class="kw">static</span> <span class="tp">FUNC</span>(<span class="tp">Std_ReturnType</span>, SUM_SPM_CODE) <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_ActivateProfile</span>(
    <span class="tp">uint16</span> ApplicationInterfaceID)
{
    <span class="tp">Std_ReturnType</span> retVal = <span class="nm">E_NOT_OK</span>;
    <span class="tp">sint16</span> PowProfIndex;

    <span class="cm">/* Guard: reject if last deactivation was for same ID (prevent race) */</span>
    <span class="kw">if</span> ((Rte_IrvRead_RE_SPM_ActivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqFlag() == <span class="nm">FALSE</span>) ||
        (Rte_IrvRead_RE_SPM_ActivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqID() != ApplicationInterfaceID))
    {
        <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">Spm_GetState</span>() != Spm_Running)
        {
            retVal = <span class="nm">E_NOT_OK</span>;   <span class="cm">/* SPM must be in Running state */</span>
        }
        <span class="kw">else</span>
        {
            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_ActivateProfile_Spm_LastActReqID(ApplicationInterfaceID);
            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_ActivateProfile_Spm_LastActReqFlag(<span class="nm">TRUE</span>);

            PowProfIndex = <span class="fn">Spm_GetPowProfIndexFromAppID</span>(ApplicationInterfaceID);
            <span class="kw">if</span> ((PowProfIndex != SPM_INVALID) &amp;&amp;
                (SPM_GET_LOC_ACT_ALLOWED_FROM_CONF(PowProfIndex) == <span class="nm">TRUE</span>))
            {
                <span class="cm">/* Check learning session is not pending */</span>
                <span class="kw">if</span> (Rte_IrvRead_Spm_Learning_Status() != SUM_LRNG_PENDING)
                {
                    <span class="cm">/* BFS dispatch: enqueue root profile + all dependencies */</span>
                    <span class="fn">Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher</span>((<span class="tp">uint8</span>)PowProfIndex, <span class="nm">0u</span>,
                                             SPM_ACT_REQ, &amp;retVal);
                }
                <span class="kw">else</span>
                {
                    <span class="cm">/* Reject: learning session in progress */</span>
                    <span class="fn">Spm_AppendFeedbackErrorItemToList</span>(
                        (<span class="tp">uint8</span>)PowProfIndex, <span class="nm">0u</span>,
                        Spm_REJECTED_PROFILE_BLOCKED, <span class="nm">0xFFFFFFFF</span>, <span class="nm">0xFF</span>);
                }
            }

            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_ActivateProfile_Spm_LastActReqFlag(<span class="nm">FALSE</span>);
        }
    }
    <span class="kw">return</span> retVal;
}</pre>
    </div>
</details>

<h3 id="section-5-2">5.2 Profile Deactivation Flow</h3>

<p>When <code>SPM_DeactivateProfile(ApplicationInterfaceID)</code> is called:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Validation</strong>: Checks profile is known, no conflicting activation in progress</li>
  <li><strong>Requester List Update</strong>: Changes the requester's <code>ReqType</code> to <code>Spm_REQ_DEACTIVATION</code></li>
  <li><strong>FSM Processing</strong>: When the FSM detects no more ACTIVATED/ACTIVATED_CONSUMED requesters:
    <ul>
      <li>Local profile: Calls <code>SrvcMgr_ActivateServices()</code> with deactivation &rarr; transitions to <strong>Inactive</strong></li>
      <li>Remote profile: Sends DEACTIVATE via SM Frame</li>
      <li>Disables PDU groups if no other profiles use them</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: SPM_DeactivateProfile &amp; BFS Dispatcher</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_Services.c</code> &mdash; the deactivation API entry point:</p>
<pre><code>FUNC(Std_ReturnType, SPM_CODE)
SPM_DeactivateProfile(VAR(uint16, AUTOMATIC) ApplicationInterfaceID) {
    Std_ReturnType retVal = E_NOT_OK;
    sint16 PowProfIndex;

    // Guard: reject if the last activation was for the same ID (prevent race condition)
    if ((Rte_IrvRead_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastActReqFlag() == FALSE) ||
        (Rte_IrvRead_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastActReqID() != ApplicationInterfaceID))
    {
        if (Spm_GetState() != Spm_Running) {
            retVal = E_NOT_OK;   // SPM must be in Running state
        } else {
            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqID(ApplicationInterfaceID);
            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqFlag(TRUE);

            PowProfIndex = Spm_GetPowProfIndexFromAppID(ApplicationInterfaceID);
            if ((PowProfIndex != SPM_INVALID) &amp;&amp;
                (SPM_GET_LOC_ACT_ALLOWED_FROM_CONF(PowProfIndex) == TRUE)) {
                Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher((uint8)PowProfIndex, 0u, SPM_DEA_REQ, &amp;retVal);
            }

            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqFlag(FALSE);
        }
    }
    return retVal;
}</code></pre>

  <p>The BFS dependency dispatcher walks all dependent profiles and enqueues them:</p>
<pre><code>void Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher(uint8 profileIndx, uint32 TrgDvcIP,
                               uint8 reqCode, Std_ReturnType* retVal) {
    boolean visited[SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM];
    SpmPrfDepLstType queue[SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM];
    uint32 front = 0u, rear = 0u;

    // Initialize visited array
    for (i = 0u; i &lt; SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM; i++) visited[i] = FALSE;

    // Enqueue root profile with MSB flag set (marks it as root)
    visited[profileIndx] = TRUE;
    queue[rear].prfDepType = SPM_PRF_DEP_ACT_AND_CONS;
    queue[rear].prfIndex = profileIndx;
    rear++;

    while (front != rear) {
        Sum_Spm_PwrPrf_Item.TrgDvcIpRequester = TrgDvcIP;
        Sum_Spm_PwrPrf_Item.reqDependencyType = queue[front].prfDepType;
        Sum_Spm_PwrPrf_Item.posOfPrfInCfgArray = queue[front].prfIndex;
        // Root flag: MSB=1 for root profile, MSB=0 for dependencies
        Sum_Spm_PwrPrf_Item.reqCode = reqCode | (uint8)(((front == 0u) ? 1u : 0u) &lt;&lt; 7u);

        if (!SPM_EnqueueRequest(&amp;Sum_Spm_RequestQueue, Sum_Spm_PwrPrf_Item)) {
            *retVal = E_NOT_OK;   // queue full!
            break;
        }

        // BFS: enqueue all unvisited dependencies of this profile
        for (indexDep = 0; indexDep &lt; PrfDepLstSize; indexDep++) {
            if (!visited[depProfile.prfIndex]) {
                visited[depProfile.prfIndex] = TRUE;
                queue[rear] = depProfile;
                rear++;
            }
        }
        front++;
    }
}</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Key insight:</strong> The BFS ensures that when you deactivate profile Rear_Closure_2 (AppIntfID=10), all its dependencies (Rear_Closure_Output, HW_Input_Analog, etc.) are also deactivated in breadth-first order. The root profile gets <code>reqCode | 0x80</code> (MSB=1) so downstream handlers know it's the original request.</p></blockquote>
</div>

<details>
    <summary>Implementation Example &mdash; Sum_Spm_DeactivateProfile (from Sum_Spm_Services.c)</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
<pre><span class="cm">/* Profile deactivation API - removes requester and dispatches BFS deactivation */</span>
<span class="kw">static</span> <span class="tp">FUNC</span>(<span class="tp">Std_ReturnType</span>, SUM_SPM_CODE) <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_DeactivateProfile</span>(
    <span class="tp">uint16</span> ApplicationInterfaceID)
{
    <span class="tp">Std_ReturnType</span> retVal = <span class="nm">E_NOT_OK</span>;
    <span class="tp">sint16</span> PowProfIndex;

    <span class="cm">/* Guard: reject if last activation was for same ID (prevent race) */</span>
    <span class="kw">if</span> ((Rte_IrvRead_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastActReqFlag() == <span class="nm">FALSE</span>) ||
        (Rte_IrvRead_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastActReqID() != ApplicationInterfaceID))
    {
        <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">Spm_GetState</span>() != Spm_Running)
        {
            retVal = <span class="nm">E_NOT_OK</span>;
        }
        <span class="kw">else</span>
        {
            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqID(ApplicationInterfaceID);
            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqFlag(<span class="nm">TRUE</span>);

            PowProfIndex = <span class="fn">Spm_GetPowProfIndexFromAppID</span>(ApplicationInterfaceID);
            <span class="kw">if</span> ((PowProfIndex != SPM_INVALID) &amp;&amp;
                (SPM_GET_LOC_ACT_ALLOWED_FROM_CONF(PowProfIndex) == <span class="nm">TRUE</span>))
            {
                <span class="cm">/* BFS dispatch: enqueue root + all dependencies for deactivation */</span>
                <span class="fn">Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher</span>((<span class="tp">uint8</span>)PowProfIndex, <span class="nm">0u</span>,
                                         SPM_DEA_REQ, &amp;retVal);
            }

            Rte_IrvWrite_RE_SPM_DeactivateProfile_Spm_LastDeactReqFlag(<span class="nm">FALSE</span>);
        }
    }
    <span class="kw">return</span> retVal;
}</pre>
    </div>
</details>

<h3 id="section-5-3">5.3 Wakeup Sequence Execution (PowerOnDevice)</h3>

<p>When a remote profile needs activation and the target ECU is OFF:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>SM triggers PM</strong>: Requests <code>PowerOnDevice()</code> for the target IP</li>
  <li><strong>PM looks up PGTT</strong>: Finds the wakeup sequence for the target device</li>
  <li><strong>Step-by-step execution</strong>:
    <ul>
      <li>For each wakeup step (ordered by <code>SpmSeqStepID</code>):
        <ul>
          <li><strong>TC10</strong>: Calls <code>EthSM_RequestComMode()</code> with wakeup request</li>
          <li><strong>ETH WUF A/B/C</strong>: Sets the bit in the Ethernet wakeup frame buffer, sends unicast</li>
          <li><strong>CAN WUF A/B/C</strong>: Sets the bit in the CAN wakeup frame buffer, sends via <code>CanIf_Transmit()</code></li>
          <li><strong>GPIO</strong>: Passes the bit buffer to the configured Helper Function</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Waits <code>SpmSeqStepDly</code> milliseconds between steps</li>
      <li>Consecutive steps with delay=0 are combined into a single transmission</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>PowerOffDevice</strong> (reverse): De-asserts bits in the same order (TC10 commands are skipped)</li>
</ol>

<details>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; TC10 Wakeup Sequence with Retry</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
        <div class="info-box note">
            <div class="box-title">Scenario</div>
            A remote ADAS radar ECU needs activation for the adaptive cruise control feature. The first wakeup attempt fails because the radar ECU does not respond with a heartbeat within the expected window. SPM retries the full PowerOnDevice sequence.
        </div>
