  <text x="310" y="546" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">or no profiles remain requested. De-assert/re-assert clears any stuck</text>
  <text x="310" y="562" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">hardware state on the remote ECU's wakeup circuitry.</text>
</svg>
    </div>
</details>

<details>
    <summary>Implementation Example &mdash; Sum_Spm_PowerOnDevice (from Sum_Spm_PowMgr.c)</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
<pre><span class="cm">/* Executes the PGTT wakeup sequence for a target device */</span>
<span class="kw">static</span> <span class="tp">FUNC</span>(<span class="kw">void</span>, SUM_SPM_CODE) <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_PowerOnDevice</span>(
    <span class="tp">uint8</span> trgDvcIdx)
{
    <span class="tp">uint8</span> stepIdx;
    <span class="tp">uint8</span> numSteps;
    <span class="kw">const</span> Spm_PgttSeqStep_Type* pgttSeq_p;

    <span class="cm">/* Look up PGTT sequence for this target device */</span>
    pgttSeq_p = Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].SpmTrgDevInfo.trgHndl_p-&gt;pgttSeq_p;
    numSteps  = Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].SpmTrgDevInfo.trgHndl_p-&gt;pgttSeqSize;

    <span class="kw">for</span> (stepIdx = <span class="nm">0u</span>; stepIdx &lt; numSteps; stepIdx++)
    {
        <span class="kw">switch</span> (pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].wakeupType)
        {
            <span class="kw">case</span> SPM_WAKEUP_TC10:
                <span class="cm">/* TC10 Ethernet physical-layer wakeup */</span>
                <span class="fn">EthSM_RequestComMode</span>(
                    pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].channelId,
                    COMM_FULL_COMMUNICATION);
                <span class="kw">break</span>;

            <span class="kw">case</span> SPM_WAKEUP_ETH_WUF_A:
            <span class="kw">case</span> SPM_WAKEUP_ETH_WUF_B:
            <span class="kw">case</span> SPM_WAKEUP_ETH_WUF_C:
                <span class="cm">/* Set bit in Ethernet wakeup frame buffer and transmit */</span>
                <span class="fn">Spm_SetWufBit</span>(
                    pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].wakeupType,
                    pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].bitPosition, <span class="nm">TRUE</span>);
                <span class="fn">Spm_TransmitWuf</span>(pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].wakeupType);
                <span class="kw">break</span>;

            <span class="kw">case</span> SPM_WAKEUP_CAN_WUF_A:
            <span class="kw">case</span> SPM_WAKEUP_CAN_WUF_B:
                <span class="cm">/* Set bit in CAN wakeup frame and transmit via CanIf */</span>
                <span class="fn">Spm_SetWufBit</span>(
                    pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].wakeupType,
                    pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].bitPosition, <span class="nm">TRUE</span>);
                <span class="fn">CanIf_Transmit</span>(pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].pduId,
                               &amp;Spm_CanWufPduInfo);
                <span class="kw">break</span>;

            <span class="kw">case</span> SPM_WAKEUP_GPIO:
                <span class="cm">/* Delegate to configured helper function */</span>
                pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].helperFnc_p(
                    pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].bitPosition, <span class="nm">TRUE</span>);
                <span class="kw">break</span>;

            <span class="kw">default</span>:
                <span class="kw">break</span>;
        }

        <span class="cm">/* Apply inter-step delay (0 = combine with next step) */</span>
        <span class="kw">if</span> (pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].stepDelay_ms &gt; <span class="nm">0u</span>)
        {
            <span class="fn">Spm_DelayMs</span>(pgttSeq_p[stepIdx].stepDelay_ms);
        }
    }
}</pre>
    </div>
</details>

<h3 id="section-5-4">5.4 PowerOnDevice Retry</h3>

<p>If a target device is in <strong>Faulted</strong> or <strong>Shutdown Pending</strong> state and has profiles still requested:</p>

<div class="hflow">
  <div class="flow-step gray">No Retry</div>
  <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step remote">PowerOff<br>Sequence<small>De-assert wakeup signals</small></div>
  <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step hl">Wait Time<small>Default 1s</small></div>
  <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step local">PowerOn<br>Sequence<small>Re-assert wakeup signals</small></div>
  <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step hl">Wait to Restart<small>Default 10s</small></div>
</div>
<p style="text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:-12px;">&#x21bb; Loops back to PowerOff if device still faulted and profiles still requested</p>

<ul>
  <li>PowerOff sequence executes first (de-assert all wakeup signals)</li>
  <li>Wait <code>SpmTrgDvcPowerOnDeviceWaitTimeBetweenOffandOnSequence</code> (default 1s)</li>
  <li>PowerOn sequence executes (re-assert wakeup signals)</li>
  <li>Wait <code>SpmTrgDvcPowerOnDeviceRetryPeriodicity</code> (default 10s) before retrying</li>
  <li>Stops when device recovers (state = On) or no more profiles requested</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="section-5-5">5.5 Shutdown Coordination</h3>

<p>SPM coordinates with SUSD via two interfaces:</p>

<h4>PermitExecution (SUSD &rarr; SPM)</h4>
<ul>
  <li>Bit mask telling SPM which functions can execute</li>
  <li>Bit 0 (Wakeups Active): SPM can run</li>
  <li>Bit 1 (Shutdown Target): When deasserted, SPM sends final full-scale HB</li>
</ul>

<h4>ShutdownPermission (SPM &rarr; SUSD)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><code>0x01..0xFD</code>: Rolling counter (SPM is active, has profiles running)</li>
  <li><code>0xFF</code>: SPM votes for shutdown (all conditions met)</li>
  <li><code>0xFE</code>: Shutdown ready (final HBs sent, SUSD can proceed)</li>
</ul>

<h4>Conditions to vote for shutdown (0xFF)</h4>
<ol>
  <li>HB Shutdown Delay after last burst HB has elapsed</li>
  <li>Own wakeup bit is not set in received WUF</li>
  <li>No local profiles are requested</li>
  <li>SpmStayAwakeTimer has elapsed</li>
  <li>No managed target devices requested by remote via WUF</li>
</ol>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: Shutdown State Machine</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_SoftwMgr.c</code> &mdash; the main function orchestrates the complete shutdown logic:</p>
<pre><code>static SPM_ShutdownPermission Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter = 0x00U;

FUNC(void, SPM_CODE) SPM_SoftMgr_MainFunction(void) {
    SPM_PermitExecution Spm_allowed = 0x00U;

    // Read PermitExecution from SUSD
    Rte_Read_RP_SUSD_SPM_PerExec_SUSD_SWC_ExecutionStatus(&amp;Spm_allowed);

    switch (SpmCtrl_Status) {
        case Spm_Running:
            // Rolling counter: cycles 0x00 &rarr; 0x01 &rarr; 0x02 &rarr; 0x03 &rarr; 0x00
            Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter = (Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter + 1u) % 0x04u;

            // Check if SUSD deasserted execution permission
            if ((Spm_allowed | SPM_PERMIT_EXEC_MASK) != SPM_EXEC_MASK_PASSED) {
                SpmCtrl_Status = Spm_PrepareToShutdown;
                Spm_ErrorHandler_ShutdownDetected();
                SPM_InitQueue(&amp;Sum_Spm_RequestQueue);   // flush pending requests
                break;
            }
            // ... (all normal handlers: LowVoltage, FSM, LoC, etc.) ...

            // Vote for shutdown (0xFF) when ALL conditions met:
            if (Sum_Spm_Shutdown_Delay_Has_Expired() &amp;&amp;           // HB delay elapsed
                !Spm_GetOwnwakeUpBit() &amp;&amp;                         // own WUF bit not set
                (Spm_GetNotInactiveLocalProfNumberForHB() == 0u) &amp;&amp;  // no active local profiles
                !Spm_IsStayAwakeTimerActive() &amp;&amp;                  // stay-awake timer expired
                !Spm_IsTargetDeviceRequestedByRemote())           // no remote WUF requests
            {
                SpmCtrl_Status = Spm_PrepareToShutdown;
            }
            break;

        case Spm_PrepareToShutdown:
            Sum_Spm_CheckHBCounterShallBeSentFullScale(Spm_allowed);
            Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter = 0xFFU;    // vote "preparing for shutdown"

            if (Sum_Spm_IsFinalHeartbeatSent()) {
                Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter = 0xFEU;  // "shutdown ready"
            }
            Spm_HandleInitAndShutdownState(Spm_allowed);
            break;
    }

    // Always write the shutdown permission to SUSD
    Rte_Write_PP_SPM_SUSD_ShutDown_SUSD_UserRequest(Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter);
}</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Key insight:</strong> SUSD reads <code>ShutdownPermission</code> every cycle. A rolling counter (0x00-0x03) proves SPM is alive. <code>0xFF</code> = "I want to shut down". <code>0xFE</code> = "final HB sent, you may power me off".</p></blockquote>
</div>

<details>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Graceful Shutdown with NvM Write-Back</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
        <div class="info-box note">
            <div class="box-title">Scenario</div>
            The vehicle is turned off after a drive. SUSD initiates shutdown. SPM has three active profiles (two local, one remote on the body controller). SPM must deactivate all, send final heartbeats, and coordinate with NvM to persist diagnostic data before allowing SUSD to power off.
        </div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 620 583" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="spm_sw7_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- Step 1: Detection / trigger -->
  <rect x="10" y="5" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="11" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f59e0b"/>
  <text x="29" y="29" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">1</text>
  <text x="52" y="22" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">T=0ms &#8212; SUSD Deasserts PermitExecution</text>
  <text x="52" y="38" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">SPM reads via RTE</text>
  <text x="52" y="52" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">SpmCtrl_Status transitions Spm_Running &#8594; Spm_PrepareToShutdown</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="71" x2="310" y2="85" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw7_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 2: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="85" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="91" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="109" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">2</text>
  <text x="52" y="102" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=5ms &#8212; Shutdown Handler Executes</text>
  <text x="52" y="118" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Flushes SPM_RequestQueue (no new activations allowed)</text>
  <text x="52" y="132" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Sends DEACTIVATE SM Frame to Body Controller for remote profile</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="151" x2="310" y2="165" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw7_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 3: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="165" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="171" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="189" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">3</text>
  <text x="52" y="182" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=50ms &#8212; Local Profiles Deactivated</text>
  <text x="52" y="198" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Seat_Position_Memory deactivated via SrvcMgr</text>
  <text x="52" y="212" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Ambient_Lighting deactivated via SrvcMgr</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="231" x2="310" y2="245" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw7_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 4: Success -->
  <rect x="10" y="245" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="251" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="269" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">4</text>
  <text x="52" y="262" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=200ms &#8212; Body Controller Acknowledges</text>
  <text x="52" y="278" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Remote profile deactivation acknowledged via SM Frame</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="297" x2="310" y2="311" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw7_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 5: Notification -->
  <rect x="10" y="311" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#fff8e6" stroke="#f39c12" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="317" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#f39c12"/>
  <text x="29" y="335" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">5</text>
  <text x="52" y="328" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#b45309">T=210ms &#8212; All Profiles Inactive, Final Heartbeat</text>
  <text x="52" y="344" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">DID 0xE0DD bitmap cleared</text>
  <text x="52" y="358" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Sum_Spm_CheckHBCounterShallBeSentFullScale() sends final full-scale heartbeat</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="377" x2="310" y2="391" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw7_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 6: Processing -->
  <rect x="10" y="391" width="600" height="52" rx="8" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="397" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#2563eb"/>
  <text x="29" y="415" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">6</text>
  <text x="52" y="408" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=250ms &#8212; Vote for Shutdown</text>
  <text x="52" y="424" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">ShutdownPermission set to 0xFF (vote for shutdown)</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="443" x2="310" y2="457" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw7_arr)"/>
  <!-- Step 7: Success -->
  <rect x="10" y="457" width="600" height="66" rx="8" fill="#dcfce7" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="463" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#22c55e"/>
  <text x="29" y="481" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">7</text>
  <text x="52" y="474" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#166534">T=300ms &#8212; Shutdown Ready</text>
  <text x="52" y="490" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">Sum_Spm_IsFinalHeartbeatSent() returns TRUE &#8594; ShutdownPermission = 0xFE</text>
  <text x="52" y="504" font-size="10" fill="#2d3436">SUSD reads 0xFE, SPM is now cleared for power-down</text>
  <line x1="310" y1="523" x2="310" y2="537" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#spm_sw7_arr)"/>
  <!-- KEY POINT -->
  <rect x="10" y="537" width="600" height="46" rx="8" fill="#f3e8ff" stroke="#a855f7" stroke-width="2"/>
  <text x="310" y="555" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">&#9733; SPM waits for all remote acknowledgments before voting 0xFF.</text>
  <text x="310" y="571" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#7c3aed">0xFF &#8594; 0xFE only after final heartbeat is physically sent.</text>
</svg>
    </div>
</details>

<details>
    <summary>Implementation Example &mdash; Sum_Spm_ShutdownHandler (from Sum_Spm_SoftwMgr.c)</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
<pre><span class="cm">/* Shutdown state handler - manages the transition from running to shutdown-ready */</span>
<span class="kw">static</span> <span class="tp">FUNC</span>(<span class="kw">void</span>, SUM_SPM_CODE) <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_ShutdownHandler</span>(
    <span class="tp">uint8</span> Spm_allowed)
{
    <span class="kw">static</span> <span class="tp">uint8</span> Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter = <span class="nm">0x00</span>;

    <span class="kw">switch</span> (SpmCtrl_Status)
    {
        <span class="kw">case</span> Spm_Running:
            <span class="cm">/* Rolling counter proves SPM is alive (0x00..0x03) */</span>
            Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter =
                (Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter + <span class="nm">1u</span>) % <span class="nm">0x04u</span>;

            <span class="cm">/* Check if SUSD revoked execution permission */</span>
            <span class="kw">if</span> ((Spm_allowed | SPM_PERMIT_EXEC_MASK) != SPM_EXEC_MASK_PASSED)
            {
                SpmCtrl_Status = Spm_PrepareToShutdown;
                <span class="fn">Spm_ErrorHandler_ShutdownDetected</span>();
                <span class="fn">SPM_InitQueue</span>(&amp;Sum_Spm_RequestQueue);
                <span class="kw">break</span>;
            }

            <span class="cm">/* Evaluate all shutdown conditions */</span>
            <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">Sum_Spm_Shutdown_Delay_Has_Expired</span>() &amp;&amp;
                !<span class="fn">Spm_GetOwnwakeUpBit</span>() &amp;&amp;
                (<span class="fn">Spm_GetNotInactiveLocalProfNumberForHB</span>() == <span class="nm">0u</span>) &amp;&amp;
                !<span class="fn">Spm_IsStayAwakeTimerActive</span>() &amp;&amp;
                !<span class="fn">Spm_IsTargetDeviceRequestedByRemote</span>())
            {
                SpmCtrl_Status = Spm_PrepareToShutdown;
            }
            <span class="kw">break</span>;

        <span class="kw">case</span> Spm_PrepareToShutdown:
            <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_CheckHBCounterShallBeSentFullScale</span>(Spm_allowed);
            Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter = <span class="nm">0xFF</span>;

            <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">Sum_Spm_IsFinalHeartbeatSent</span>())
            {
                Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter = <span class="nm">0xFE</span>;
            }
            <span class="fn">Spm_HandleInitAndShutdownState</span>(Spm_allowed);
            <span class="kw">break</span>;

        <span class="kw">default</span>:
            <span class="kw">break</span>;
    }

    <span class="cm">/* Always report shutdown status to SUSD */</span>
    Rte_Write_PP_SPM_SUSD_ShutDown_SUSD_UserRequest(Spm_ShutdownRollingCounter);
}</pre>
    </div>
</details>

<h3 id="section-5-6">5.6 Loss-of-Communication Handling</h3>

<h4>With a Requester (remote ECU that requested our profiles)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><code>Spm_LoC_wRequester_Handler()</code> scans requester lists for all local profiles</li>
  <li>Checks each remote requester's device power state</li>
  <li>If requester is in <strong>Faulted</strong> or <strong>Reboot</strong> state:
    <ul>
      <li>Sends error feedback via SM frame (REJECTED_LOSS_OF_HEARTBEAT or REJECTED_RESET_DETECTED)</li>
      <li>Removes the requester from the list</li>
      <li>Sets SpmStayAwakeTimer</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h4>Loss-of-Node DTC</h4>
<ul>
  <li>When a device transitions to <strong>Faulted</strong>: <code>Sum_Spm_WriteLossofNode()</code> sends the DTC base ID to SSFM</li>
  <li>When a device recovers: sends RECOVERED status</li>
</ul>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: LoC Handler &mdash; Detecting Faulted Requesters</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_SoftwMgr.c</code> &mdash; iterates all profiles and their requester lists:</p>
<pre><code>static void Spm_LoC_wRequester_Handler(void) {
    uint16 pp_idx;
    uint8  td_idx;
    SpmDevicePowerStateCode dvc_pow_state_ret;
    Spm_DevicePowerStateInfo ds_read;

    // Read device power state snapshot
    Rte_IrvRead_SPM_RE_SPM_SoftMgr_MainFunction_Spm_DevicePowerState(&amp;ds_read);

    // For each power profile...
    for (pp_idx = 0; pp_idx &lt; SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM; pp_idx++) {
        // For each requester of this profile...
        for (td_idx = 0; td_idx &lt; SPM_PrfStsMgr_RAM[pp_idx].reqLst.size; td_idx++) {

            // Skip if already deactivated or null
            boolean is_inactive = (reqLst[td_idx].ReqType == SPM_NULL_REQ) ||
                                  (reqLst[td_idx].ReqType == SPM_REQ_DEACTIVATION);

            if (!is_inactive &amp;&amp; reqLst[td_idx].requesterIP != 0UL) {
                // Check requester's device power state
                dvc_pow_state_ret = Spm_DevicePowerStateParser(reqLst[td_idx].requesterIP, &amp;ds_read);

                if (dvc_pow_state_ret == SPM_Faulted || dvc_pow_state_ret == SPM_Reboot) {
                    // Choose error code based on state
                    uint8 err_code = (dvc_pow_state_ret == SPM_Faulted)
                        ? Spm_REJECTED_LOSS_OF_HEARTBEAT    // 0x15
                        : Spm_REJECTED_RESET_DETECTED;       // 0x16

                    // Queue error feedback to notify the (dead) requester
                    Spm_AppendFeedbackErrorItemToList(pp_idx, requesterIP, err_code, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFF);

                    // Remove requester from list
                    reqLst[td_idx].ReqType = SPM_NULL_REQ;

                    // Keep local profiles awake to allow recovery
                    if (SPM_GET_PROF_IS_LOC_FROM_CONF(pp_idx)) {
                        Spm_StartStayAwakeTimer();
                    }
                }

                if (dvc_pow_state_ret == SPM_UnknownDevice) {
                    reqLst[td_idx].ReqType = SPM_NULL_REQ;  // unknown device, remove
                }
            }
        }
    }
}</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Key insight:</strong> The error feedback is queued via <code>Spm_AppendFeedbackErrorItemToList()</code> and later sent via the SM Frame. The <code>StayAwakeTimer</code> ensures the ECU doesn't shut down immediately &mdash; it stays on long enough for the faulted requester to potentially reboot and re-request.</p></blockquote>
</div>

<details>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Heartbeat Loss Triggering Profile Failover</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
