<details>
    <summary>Implementation Example &mdash; Sum_Spm_HeartbeatMonitor (from Sum_Spm_PowMgr.c)</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
<pre><span class="cm">/* Periodic heartbeat monitor - checks all target devices for HB counter changes */</span>
<span class="kw">static</span> <span class="tp">FUNC</span>(<span class="kw">void</span>, SUM_SPM_CODE) <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_HeartbeatMonitor</span>(<span class="kw">void</span>)
{
    <span class="tp">uint8</span> trgDvcIdx;
    <span class="tp">uint32</span> currentHbCnt;
    <span class="tp">uint32</span> previousHbCnt;
    Spm_DevicePowerStateCode currentState;

    <span class="kw">for</span> (trgDvcIdx = <span class="nm">0u</span>; trgDvcIdx &lt; SPM_CONF_TRG_DVC_NUM; trgDvcIdx++)
    {
        currentState = Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].devicePowerState;
        currentHbCnt = Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].receivedHbCounter;
        previousHbCnt = Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].lastCheckedHbCounter;

        <span class="kw">if</span> (currentState == SPM_DeviceOn)
        {
            <span class="kw">if</span> (currentHbCnt == previousHbCnt)
            {
                <span class="cm">/* HB counter did not increment */</span>
                Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].noHbCnt++;

                <span class="kw">if</span> (Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].noHbCnt &gt;=
                    SPM_HB_LOSS_THRESHOLD)
                {
                    <span class="cm">/* Threshold reached: transition to Faulted */</span>
                    Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].devicePowerState =
                        SPM_Faulted;

                    <span class="cm">/* Notify SSFM for DTC reporting */</span>
                    <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_WriteLossofNode</span>(
                        Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].trgDvcIp,
                        SPM_NODE_LOST);
                }
            }
            <span class="kw">else</span>
            {
                <span class="cm">/* HB counter incremented: device is alive */</span>
                Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].noHbCnt = <span class="nm">0u</span>;
                Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].lastCheckedHbCounter =
                    currentHbCnt;
            }
        }
        <span class="kw">else</span> <span class="kw">if</span> (currentState == SPM_Faulted)
        {
            <span class="cm">/* Check if device is recovering (HB counter changed) */</span>
            <span class="kw">if</span> (currentHbCnt != previousHbCnt)
            {
                Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].devicePowerState =
                    SPM_Reboot;
                Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].noHbCnt = <span class="nm">0u</span>;

                <span class="cm">/* Notify SSFM: device recovered */</span>
                <span class="fn">Sum_Spm_WriteLossofNode</span>(
                    Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[trgDvcIdx].trgDvcIp,
                    SPM_NODE_RECOVERED);
            }
        }
    }
}</pre>
    </div>
</details>

<h3 id="section-5-7">5.7 Low Voltage Battery Priority</h3>

<p>SPM enforces energy-aware activation:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Each profile has priority levels for Vehicle ON (<code>SpmVehDefActPriorON</code>) and Vehicle OFF (<code>SpmVehDefActPriorOFF</code>)</li>
  <li>SPM receives the current priority threshold from the Vehicle Energy Optimizer via SSFM</li>
  <li>If a profile's priority is below the threshold, activation is refused (REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER)</li>
  <li><code>Spm_ErrorHandler_LowVoltageBattery()</code> periodically checks if active profiles still meet the threshold</li>
</ul>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: Low Voltage Battery Priority Check</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_ErrorHandler.c</code> &mdash; periodic check for every profile:</p>
<pre><code>// Called every SM main cycle when branded
void Spm_ErrorHandler_LowVoltageBattery(void) {
    for (i = 0u; i &lt; SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM; i++) {
        if (FALSE == Spm_Get_ActivationAvailabilityLowVoltageBatteryPriority(i)) {
            Spm_SendDeactivationRequestForEachRequester(i, Spm_REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER);
        }
    }
}

// Per-profile priority evaluation
static boolean Spm_Get_ActivationAvailabilityLowVoltageBatteryPriority(uint8 powProfIndex) {
    boolean ret = TRUE;

    // Only local profiles are affected by low voltage
    if (SPM_GET_PROF_IS_LOC_FROM_CONF(powProfIndex) == TRUE) {
        Rte_Read_RP_SUSD_SPM_VehiclePowerMode_VehiclePowerMode(&amp;VehPowMode);

        if (VehPowMode == OFF) {
            // Compare Vehicle OFF priority against current threshold
            if (SPM_GET_LOWVOLTAGEPRIORITY_VEHOFF(powProfIndex) != SPM_NOT_APPLICABLE) {
                ret = (SPM_GET_LOWVOLTAGEPRIORITY_VEHOFF(powProfIndex) &lt;= Spm_GetPriorityLevelValue())
                    ? FALSE : TRUE;   // &lt;= threshold means "not enough power"
            }
        } else {
            // Compare Vehicle ON priority against current threshold
            if (SPM_GET_LOWVOLTAGEPRIORITY_VEHON(powProfIndex) != SPM_NOT_APPLICABLE) {
                ret = (SPM_GET_LOWVOLTAGEPRIORITY_VEHON(powProfIndex) &lt;= Spm_GetPriorityLevelValue())
                    ? FALSE : TRUE;
            }
        }
    }
    return ret;  // TRUE = can stay active, FALSE = must deactivate
}</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Example:</strong> Profile Rear_Closure_HW_Input_LIN has <code>PriorityON=MEDIUM</code> and <code>PriorityOFF=MEDIUM</code>. If VEO reports the current threshold is <code>HIGH</code>, then MEDIUM &le; HIGH evaluates to TRUE &rarr; <code>ret = FALSE</code> &rarr; the profile gets deactivated with <code>REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER</code>.</p></blockquote>
</div>

<details>
    <summary>Scenario Walkthrough &mdash; Battery Shedding During Cold Start</summary>
    <div class="details-content">
        <div class="info-box note">
            <div class="box-title">Scenario</div>
            A vehicle in a cold climate (-20&deg;C) is started. The cranking load drops battery voltage significantly. The Vehicle Energy Optimizer (VEO) progressively raises the priority threshold, and SPM must shed profiles in priority order while protecting safety-critical functions.
        </div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 620 617" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="spm_sw9_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- Step 1: Initial state -->
  <rect x="10" y="5" width="600" height="80" rx="8" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="16" y="11" width="26" height="26" rx="13" fill="#3b82f6"/>
  <text x="29" y="29" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">1</text>
  <text x="52" y="22" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#1e40af">T=0s &#8212; Ignition ON, Normal Voltage</text>
