<h3 id="section-5-8">5.8 Variant Management</h3>

<p>SPM supports <strong>branded/unbranded</strong> vehicle variants:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>Sum_Spm_VariantManagement</code> module handles variant-specific behavior</li>
  <li>In <strong>Unbranded</strong> state: HB is not sent, wakeup reception logic differs</li>
  <li>Runtime variant configuration via <code>Rte_Call_SPM_RP_SPM_GetDeviceVariantInfo_setVariant</code></li>
</ul>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: Variant Detection &amp; Data Structure Population</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_VariantManagement.c</code> &mdash; called every SM cycle until branded:</p>
<pre><code>static boolean SPM_IsBranded = FALSE;   // starts as unbranded

void Sum_Spm_GetVariantId_DataStructurePopulation_WithVariant(void) {
    uint8 variantInfo_u8 = 0U;

    if (FALSE == Sum_Spm_GetIsBranded()) {
        // Ask SrvcMgr for the device variant (1-based index)
        if (RTE_E_SWC_GetDeviceVariantInfo_E_OK ==
            Rte_Call_RP_SPM_GetDeviceVariantInfo_setVariant(&amp;variantInfo_u8))
        {
            if ((variantInfo_u8 &gt; 0u) &amp;&amp; (variantInfo_u8 &lt;= SUM_SPM_NUMBER_OF_VARIANTS)) {
                // Populate network config for this variant
                for (i = 0u; i &lt; SUM_SPM_NUMBER_OF_NET_CONF; i++) {
                    SPM_NetworkInfo_Wrap[i] = Spm_NetworkInfo_Wrap_PerVariant[variantInfo_u8 - 1u][i];
                }
                // Set active wakeup frame info for this variant
                Spm_ActiveWkupFrameInfo_p = Spm_WkupFrameInfo_PerVariant[variantInfo_u8 - 1u];
                Sum_Spm_SetVariantId(variantInfo_u8 - 1u);
                // Set target device handling info for this variant
                if (TrgHndlInfo_SpmTrgDvc_PerVariant[variantInfo_u8 - 1u] != NULL_PTR) {
                    Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[0].SpmTrgDevInfo.trgHndl_p =
                        TrgHndlInfo_SpmTrgDvc_PerVariant[variantInfo_u8 - 1u];
                }
                Sum_Spm_SetIsBranded(TRUE);   // &larr; from now on, full PM functions are active
            }
        }
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>In the SM main function, branded vs unbranded determines which handlers run:</p>
<pre><code>case Spm_Running:
    if (FALSE == Sum_Spm_GetIsBranded()) {
        // UNBRANDED: only try to detect variant each cycle
        Sum_Spm_GetVariantId_DataStructurePopulation_WithVariant();
    } else {
        // BRANDED: full power management
        Spm_ErrorHandler_LowVoltageBattery();
        Spm_ReadIncoming_SM_Message();
        Spm_ErrorHandler_VehOff();
        Spm_DequeueReqActionHandler();
        Spm_LoC_wRequester_Handler();
        Spm_FSMManger();
        // ... all other handlers ...
    }</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Key insight:</strong> An unbranded ECU does NOT send heartbeats, does NOT process wakeup frames normally, and does NOT handle profile activation. It only listens for its variant assignment. Once branded, all data structures (network info, wakeup frame info, target device handling) are populated for that specific variant.</p></blockquote>
</div>

<h3 id="section-5-9">5.9 Learning Session Management</h3>

<p>When Service Discovery runs a learning session:</p>
<ul>
  <li>SrvcMgr notifies SPM via <code>Runnable_SPM_SdLearningStatusIndication()</code></li>
  <li><strong>PENDING</strong>: SPM deactivates all active profiles, rejects new activations (REJECTED_PROFILE_BLOCKED)</li>
  <li><strong>SUCCESSFUL/FAILED</strong>: SPM queries SD for updated node IP addresses (<code>Sd_GetNodeAddress()</code>)</li>
</ul>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: Learning Session State Machine</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_Services.c</code> &mdash; handles learning status transitions:</p>
<pre><code>Runnable_SPM_SdLearningStatusIndication(SPM_SDLearningStatus learningStatus) {
    SPM_SDLearningStatus previousStatus =
        Rte_IrvRead_RE_SPM_SrvcMgr_SdLearningStatusIndication_Spm_Learning_Status();

    // Transition: NOT_PENDING &rarr; PENDING (learning session starts)
    if (SUM_LRNG_PENDING == learningStatus &amp;&amp; SUM_LRNG_PENDING != previousStatus) {
        // Block activations immediately by updating IRV first
        Rte_IrvWrite_..._Spm_Learning_Status(learningStatus);

        // Deactivate ALL active profiles (reject with PROFILE_BLOCKED)
        for (i = 0u; i &lt; SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM; i++) {
            Spm_SendDeactivationRequestForEachRequester(i, Spm_REJECTED_PROFILE_BLOCKED);
        }

        // Process the deactivation queue immediately
        Spm_DequeueReqActionHandler();
        Spm_FSMManger();
        Spm_SoftwMgr_PopulateSMFrame();
    }
    // Transition: PENDING &rarr; SUCCESSFUL/FAILED (learning session ends)
    else if (SUM_LRNG_PENDING == previousStatus &amp;&amp; SUM_LRNG_PENDING != learningStatus) {
        // Re-query SD for updated target device IPs
        SPM_PM_Init_ProfilesStructs();   // calls Sd_GetNodeAddress() for each profile

        // Only NOW allow activations again
        Rte_IrvWrite_..._Spm_Learning_Status(learningStatus);
    }
    else {
        Rte_IrvWrite_..._Spm_Learning_Status(learningStatus);
    }
}</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Why this matters:</strong> During a learning session, Service Discovery re-discovers all services on the network. Target device IPs may change. SPM must deactivate everything, wait for SD to finish, then re-populate its profile-to-IP mappings via <code>Sd_GetNodeAddress()</code> before allowing new activations. The order matters &mdash; the IRV is updated <strong>before</strong> deactivation in the PENDING case (to block concurrent threads) but <strong>after</strong> IP re-query in the completion case.</p></blockquote>
</div>

<details>
