<h3 id="section-5-10">5.10 WUF Rolling Buffer</h3>

<p>For intermediate nodes handling incoming wakeup frames:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Frames are stored in a rolling buffer to preserve data across processing cycles</li>
  <li><code>Sum_Spm_WufRollingBuffer</code> module manages the buffer</li>
  <li>Ensures wake-up bits from multiple received frames are combined (OR logic) before transmission</li>
</ul>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: WUF Rolling Buffer &mdash; Design &amp; Implementation</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_WufRollingBuffer.h</code> &mdash; buffer structure:</p>
<pre><code>// Design: 6 slots x 75ms = 450ms max, 375ms min validity
// A WUF received at start of slot survives 5 further rotations (375ms) before discard
#define SPM_WUF_NUM_SLOTS       (6U)
#define SPM_WUF_SLOT_PERIOD_MS  (75U)
#define SPM_WUF_SLOT_TICKS      (SPM_WUF_SLOT_PERIOD_MS / SUM_SPM_PERIOD_PM_MAINFUNCTION_MS)  // 75/5 = 15

// One time slot holds the OR-aggregate of all WUFs received during that 75ms window
typedef struct {
    uint8 WufA[WAKEUP_FRAME_LEN];   // 8 bytes
    uint8 WufB[WAKEUP_FRAME_LEN];
    uint8 WufC[WAKEUP_FRAME_LEN];
} Spm_WufSlot_Type;

typedef struct {
    Sum_Algo_Deque   deque;                              // front=oldest, back=write slot
    Spm_WufSlot_Type slotMemory[SPM_WUF_NUM_SLOTS];     // backing memory
} Spm_WufRollingBuffer_Type;</code></pre>

  <p><strong>Store incoming WUF</strong> &mdash; OR-accumulate into the write slot (deque back):</p>
<pre><code>static void Spm_WufRollingBuffer_AccumulateAndWriteSlots(const uint8* Wuf_A, ...) {
    Spm_WufSlot_Type writeSlot;
    Sum_Algo_Deque_GetAt(&amp;Spm_WufBuffer.deque, SPM_WUF_NUM_SLOTS - 1u, &amp;writeSlot);

    for (byte = 0u; byte &lt; WAKEUP_FRAME_LEN; byte++) {
        writeSlot.WufA[byte] |= Wuf_A[byte];   // OR accumulation!
        writeSlot.WufB[byte] |= Wuf_B[byte];
        writeSlot.WufC[byte] |= Wuf_C[byte];
    }

    Sum_Algo_Deque_SetAt(&amp;Spm_WufBuffer.deque, SPM_WUF_NUM_SLOTS - 1u, &amp;writeSlot);
}</code></pre>

  <p><strong>Slot rotation</strong> &mdash; every 75ms, discard oldest and add fresh empty slot:</p>
<pre><code>void Sum_Spm_WufRollingBuffer_CheckAndShiftWufSlot(void) {
    if (Spm_WufSlotTickCounter &gt; 0u)
        Spm_WufSlotTickCounter--;

    if (0u == Spm_WufSlotTickCounter) {
        // Discard oldest slot (front) and push fresh empty slot (back)
        Sum_Algo_Deque_PopFront(&amp;Spm_WufBuffer.deque, &amp;discardedSlot);
        Sum_Algo_Deque_PushBack(&amp;Spm_WufBuffer.deque, &amp;emptySlot);
        Spm_WufSlotTickCounter = SPM_WUF_SLOT_TICKS;   // reset to 15 ticks
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p><strong>Bit check</strong> &mdash; aggregates across ALL live slots for a given bit position:</p>
<pre><code>boolean Sum_Spm_WufRollingBuffer_IsBitXInWufYSet(uint8 bitPositionX, uint8 typeOfFrame) {
    uint8 byteIdx = bitPositionX &gt;&gt; 3u;            // byte = bit / 8
    uint8 bitMask = 1u &lt;&lt; (bitPositionX &amp; 0x07u);  // mask = 1 &lt;&lt; (bit % 8)
    uint8 aggregate = 0u;

    for (idx = 0u; idx &lt; SPM_WUF_NUM_SLOTS; idx++) {
        Sum_Algo_Deque_GetAt(&amp;buffer.deque, idx, &amp;slot);
        aggregate |= Spm_GetFrameByteFromSlot(&amp;slot, byteIdx, typeOfFrame);
    }

    return (aggregate &amp; bitMask) != 0u;  // TRUE if bit set in ANY slot
}</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Why a rolling buffer?</strong> WUF reception and processing happen at different rates. The buffer ensures that a wakeup bit received at any point within a ~375-450ms window is visible to all consumers (device power state, shutdown coordination). Without it, a WUF could be processed and cleared before the PM main function reads it.</p></blockquote>
</div>

<hr>

<!-- Section 6 -->
<!-- Practical Examples Section -->
<h2 id="section-examples">Practical Examples &amp; Walkthroughs</h2>

<p>This section uses <strong>real data from the current SPM configuration</strong> to walk through concrete activation scenarios, dependency resolution, SM frame exchanges, and error handling.</p>

<!-- Example: Profile Configuration -->
<h3 id="ex-profile-config">Example: Real Profile Configuration</h3>

<p>The current project has <strong>6 configured power profiles</strong>. Here is how they are set up (from <code>spm.arxml</code>):</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Profile Name</th><th>AppIntfID</th><th>Service ID</th><th>Prof #</th><th>Local?</th><th>Priority ON</th><th>Priority OFF</th><th>VehOff Timeout</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>Rear_Closure_2</strong></td><td>10</td><td>2341</td><td>0</td><td style="color:#d63031">Remote</td><td>CRITICAL</td><td>CRITICAL</td><td>100 ms</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Rear_Closure_Output</strong></td><td>11</td><td>2348</td><td>2</td><td style="color:#d63031">Remote</td><td>LOW</td><td>LOW</td><td>0 ms</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Rear_Closure_HW_Input_Analog</strong></td><td>12</td><td>2840</td><td>13</td><td style="color:#d63031">Remote</td><td>HIGH</td><td>HIGH</td><td>0 ms</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Rear_Closure_HW_Input_LIN</strong></td><td>15</td><td>2850</td><td>244</td><td style="color:#00b894">Local</td><td>MEDIUM</td><td>MEDIUM</td><td>10 ms</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Rear_Closure_HW_Output</strong></td><td>14</td><td>2850</td><td>123</td><td style="color:#00b894">Local</td><td>MEDIUM</td><td>LOW</td><td>200 ms</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Rear_Closure_Remote_3</strong></td><td>15</td><td>2884</td><td>125</td><td style="color:#d63031">Remote</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<blockquote>
  <p><strong>Key observation:</strong> Out of 6 profiles, only 2 are <strong>local</strong> (services running on this ECU). The other 4 are <strong>remote</strong> (services running on other ECUs that this SPM must coordinate with).</p>
</blockquote>

<p><strong>How Service ID is stored:</strong> The <code>SpmSrvcAndInstID</code> field packs both ServiceID and InstanceID into a single <code>uint32</code>. The upper 16 bits are the Service ID and the lower 16 bits are the Instance ID:</p>

<pre><code>// Example: SpmSrvcAndInstID = 186777600 (0x0B220B20)
//   ServiceID  = (186777600 >> 16) & 0xFFFF = 0x0B22 = 2850
//   InstanceID = 186777600 & 0xFFFF         = 0x0B20 = 45600</code></pre>

<!-- Example: Dependency Graph -->
<h3 id="ex-dependency-graph">Example: Dependency Graph</h3>

<p>Profiles don't exist in isolation &mdash; they have <strong>dependencies</strong>. When you activate a profile, SPM automatically activates all its dependencies too. Here are the real dependency chains:</p>

<!-- Dependency Chain 1 -->
<p style="font-weight:700;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Chain 1: Rear_Closure_2</p>
<div class="dep-tree">
  <div class="dep-root">Rear_Closure_2 <span style="opacity:.7;font-weight:400;margin-left:8px;">AppIntfID=10 &middot; REMOTE</span></div>
  <div class="dep-children">
    <div class="dep-child">
      <div class="dep-line"></div>
      <div class="dep-badge">ACT_AND_CONS</div>
      <div class="dep-node-remote">Rear_Closure_HW_Input_Analog <span style="font-weight:400;margin-left:6px;font-size:11px;">AppIntfID=12 &middot; REMOTE</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="dep-child">
      <div class="dep-line"></div>
      <div class="dep-badge" style="background:#0984e3;">ACTIVATED</div>
      <div class="dep-node-local">Rear_Closure_HW_Input_LIN <span style="font-weight:400;margin-left:6px;font-size:11px;">AppIntfID=15 &middot; LOCAL</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Dependency Chain 2 -->
<p style="font-weight:700;font-size:14px;margin:20px 0 8px;color:var(--primary);">Chain 2: Rear_Closure_Output</p>
<div class="dep-tree">
  <div class="dep-root">Rear_Closure_Output <span style="opacity:.7;font-weight:400;margin-left:8px;">AppIntfID=11 &middot; REMOTE</span></div>
  <div class="dep-children">
    <div class="dep-child">
      <div class="dep-line"></div>
      <div class="dep-badge" style="background:#636e72;">CONSUMED</div>
      <div class="dep-node-local">Rear_Closure_HW_Output <span style="font-weight:400;margin-left:6px;font-size:11px;">AppIntfID=14 &middot; LOCAL</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h4>What the dependency types mean in practice</h4>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Type</th><th>Activate Service?</th><th>Enable PDU Group?</th><th>Example Use Case</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>ACT_AND_CONS</code></td><td style="color:#00b894">Yes</td><td style="color:#00b894">Yes</td><td>Need the service running AND its communication channel open</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ACTIVATED</code></td><td style="color:#00b894">Yes</td><td style="color:#d63031">No</td><td>Need the service running but communication is already available</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>CONSUMED</code></td><td style="color:#d63031">No</td><td style="color:#00b894">Yes</td><td>Don't need the service itself, just enable the communication path</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<!-- Example: Local Activation -->
<h3 id="ex-local-activation">Walkthrough: Activating a Local Profile</h3>

<p>Let's trace what happens when a local SWC activates <strong>Rear_Closure_HW_Output</strong> (AppIntfID=14, Local profile, ServiceID=2850, ProfileNumber=123).</p>

<div class="flow">
  <div class="flow-step" style="background:#6c5ce7;color:white;border-color:#6c5ce7;">Application SWC<small style="color:#ddd">SPM_ActivateProfile(14)</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step">Validate Request<small>SPM Running? Allowed? LV Priority? Learning?</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step">BFS Dispatch<small>Enqueue profile + dependencies to Request Queue</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-label">Next SM cycle</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step">Dequeue &amp; Populate Requester List<small>Add IP=0 (local) to RequesterList[4]</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step hl">Local FSM: Inactive &rarr; Activating &rarr; Activated<small>SrvcMgr_ActivateServices() + BswM PDU group enable</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step local">Service Active<small>Service 2850 running, notification published to SSFM</small></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h4>Step 1: Application calls the API</h4>
<pre><code>// An application SWC calls:
SPM_ActivateProfile(14);   // AppIntfID = 14 (Rear_Closure_HW_Output)</code></pre>

<h4>Step 2: SPM validates the request</h4>
<pre><code>FUNC(Std_ReturnType, SPM_CODE)
SPM_ActivateProfile(VAR(uint16, AUTOMATIC) ApplicationInterfaceID)
{
    // 1. Map AppIntfID to profile index
    PowProfIndex = Spm_GetPowProfIndexFromAppID(14);  // returns index 4

    // 2. Validate activation is allowed:
    //    - Is SPM in Running state?
    //    - Is SpmLocActivationAllowed == TRUE for this profile?
    //    - Is low voltage battery priority met? (MEDIUM vs threshold)
    //    - Is learning session NOT pending?
    //    - Is Vehicle OFF timeout > 0? (200ms &gt; 0, OK)
    Spm_Get_ActivationAvailabilityForLocalRequest(4);  // returns TRUE

    // 3. Extract ServiceID and ProfileNumber from config
    ServiceID = SPM_GET_SW_ID_FROM_CONF(4) >> 16u;  // = 2850
    ProfileNum = SPM_GET_POW_PROF_NUMBER_FROM_CONF(4);  // = 123
    ...
}</code></pre>

<h4>Step 3: Request dispatcher enqueues the profile</h4>
<pre><code>// Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher uses BFS to enqueue profile + dependencies
//
// For Rear_Closure_HW_Output (index 4):
//   - No dependencies configured
//   - Only the root profile itself is enqueued

Request Queue after dispatch:
+-------+------------------+----------+-----------+
| Index | Profile          | ReqCode  | RequesterIP|
+-------+------------------+----------+-----------+
|   0   | HW_Output (idx4) | ACT+ROOT | 0 (local) |
+-------+------------------+----------+-----------+</code></pre>

<h4>Step 4: Dequeue handler processes the request</h4>
<pre><code>// In RE_SPM_SoftMgr_MainFunction (next SM cycle):
Spm_DequeueReqActionHandler()
  |
  +--&gt; Spm_RequesterList_ActivationRequestHandler(profileIndex=4, IP=0)
       // Adds IP=0 (local) to the requester list of profile 4
       // RequesterList[4] = [{IP=0, ReqType=ACTIVATED}]</code></pre>

<h4>Step 5: Local FSM transitions the profile</h4>
<pre><code>// Spm_LocalPowerProfile_FSM(index=4) runs:
//
// 1. Check requester list:
PresentReq = Spm_RetrieveDependencyTypeFromRequesterList(4);
// returns: Spm_ONLY_ACTIVATED_REQ_PRESENT (IP=0 is requesting activation)

// 2. State transition: Inactive --evActivationRequest--&gt; Activating
SPM_PrfStsMgr_RAM[4].sm = SPM_Activating;

// 3. Call Service Manager to activate:
Spm_ActivateServiceSrvcMgrHandlerFunction(4, TRUE);
//   --&gt; Internally calls SrvcMgr with service list:
//      spmSrvLst[4] = {pp_sID=2850, is_active=TRUE}

// 4. If SrvcMgr returns OK:
//    State transition: Activating --evActivationComplete--&gt; Activated
SPM_PrfStsMgr_RAM[4].sm = SPM_Activated;

// 5. Enable PDU groups via BswM mode switch
//    Rte_Switch_PP_SPM_ComIpduGroup_*(...)</code></pre>

<h4>Step 6: Service notification published</h4>
<pre><code>// Spm_SrvcMgrIf_HandleSrvcMgrComm() sends the active service list:
//   ServiceIDList = [2850]   // Only service 2850 is active
//   ListLength = 1
//   DTCAllowed = [TRUE]
// Published via: Rte_Write_PP_SPM_SrvcMgr_Notif_StatusNotification()</code></pre>
</div>

<!-- Example: Remote Activation with Dependencies -->
<h3 id="ex-remote-activation">Walkthrough: Remote Profile Activation with Dependencies</h3>

<p>Now let's trace the more complex scenario: activating <strong>Rear_Closure_2</strong> (AppIntfID=10, Remote), which has <strong>two dependencies</strong>.</p>

<div class="flow">
  <div class="flow-step" style="background:#6c5ce7;color:white;border-color:#6c5ce7;">Application SWC<small style="color:#ddd">SPM_ActivateProfile(10)</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step">Validate &amp; BFS Dispatch<small>Enqueue Rear_Closure_2 + 2 dependencies</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step">Populate Requester Lists<small>RequesterList[0], [2], [3] updated with IP=0</small></div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-label">FSM evaluates each profile type</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="fork">
    <div class="fork-branch">
      <div class="flow-step local" style="min-width:200px">LOCAL: HW_Input_LIN<small>Inactive &rarr; Activated<br>via SrvcMgr on this ECU</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fork-branch">
      <div class="flow-step remote" style="min-width:200px">REMOTE: Rear_Closure_2<small>Target 12.10.2.2</small></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow" style="border-color:#d63031"></div>
      <div class="flow-step" style="font-size:12px">Target OFF?<small>Yes &rarr; PowerOnDevice (wakeup)<br>No &rarr; Send SM Frame</small></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
      <div class="flow-step hl" style="font-size:12px">SM Frame: ACTIVATE<small>Wait for OK_ACTIVATION feedback</small></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
      <div class="flow-step local" style="font-size:12px">Activated<small>Remote confirmed</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fork-branch">
      <div class="flow-step remote" style="min-width:200px">REMOTE: HW_Input_Analog<small>Target 12.10.2.3</small></div>
      <div class="flow-arrow"></div>
      <div class="flow-step hl" style="font-size:12px">Same remote flow<small>PowerOn + SM Frame</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h4>Step 1: Application calls the API</h4>
<pre><code>SPM_ActivateProfile(10);   // AppIntfID = 10 (Rear_Closure_2, REMOTE)</code></pre>

<h4>Step 2: BFS Dependency Resolution</h4>
<pre><code>// Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher performs Breadth-First Search:
//
// Start: Enqueue Rear_Closure_2 (root)
// Visit Rear_Closure_2: found 2 dependencies
//   +-- Rear_Closure_HW_Input_Analog (ACT_AND_CONS) -&gt; enqueue
//   +-- Rear_Closure_HW_Input_LIN (ACTIVATED)        -&gt; enqueue
// Visit Rear_Closure_HW_Input_Analog: no further deps
// Visit Rear_Closure_HW_Input_LIN: no further deps
// BFS complete.

Request Queue after BFS dispatch:
+-------+------------------------------+-----------+-----------+
| Index | Profile                      | ReqCode   | IP        |
+-------+------------------------------+-----------+-----------+
|   0   | Rear_Closure_2 (idx 0)       | ACT+ROOT  | 0 (local) |
|   1   | HW_Input_Analog (idx 2)      | ACT       | 0 (local) |
|   2   | HW_Input_LIN (idx 3)         | ACT       | 0 (local) |
+-------+------------------------------+-----------+-----------+

// Note: ROOT flag (MSB of reqCode) is set only for the original request.
// Dependencies get reqCode without ROOT flag.</code></pre>

<h4>Step 3: Requester lists populated</h4>
<pre><code>// Spm_DequeueReqActionHandler processes each queue item:

RequesterList[0] (Rear_Closure_2):
  [{IP=0, ReqType=ACTIVATED, Feedback=NOT_SENT}]

RequesterList[2] (HW_Input_Analog):
  [{IP=0, ReqType=ACT_AND_CONS}]

RequesterList[3] (HW_Input_LIN):
  [{IP=0, ReqType=ACTIVATED}]</code></pre>

<h4>Step 4: FSM processes each profile differently</h4>
<pre><code>// === LOCAL PROFILES (processed by Spm_LocalPowerProfile_FSM) ===

// HW_Input_LIN (index 3, LOCAL):
//   Inactive --&gt; Activating --&gt; Activated
//   Calls SrvcMgr_ActivateServices() directly on this ECU
//   spmSrvLst[3] = {pp_sID=2850, is_active=TRUE}

// === REMOTE PROFILES (processed by Spm_RemotePowerProfile_FSM) ===

// Rear_Closure_2 (index 0, REMOTE, target: 12.10.2.2):
//   1. Check DevicePowerState of target 12.10.2.2
//   2. If target is OFF:
//        --&gt; Call Spm_PowerOnDevice(IP=12.10.2.2)
//        --&gt; Execute wakeup sequence (see wakeup example below)
//        --&gt; Wait for heartbeat from target
//   3. If target is ON:
//        --&gt; Send ACTIVATE command via SM Frame
//        SPM_PrfStsMgr_RAM[0].CommandSend = 0x01u;  // ACTIVATE

// HW_Input_Analog (index 2, REMOTE, target: 12.10.2.3):
//   Same remote flow as above for its target device</code></pre>

<h4>Step 5: SM Frame sent to remote ECU</h4>
<pre><code>// SPM builds an SM Frame for target 12.10.2.2:
SM Frame (Tx):
+--------------------------------------------------+
| PMSrcId  = 12.10.2.1  (our IP)                   |
| PMDestId = 12.10.2.2  (target IP)                |
+--------------------------------------------------+
| PR_MsgType = 0x00 (PROFILE_REQUEST)              |
| Size_Indicator = 1                               |
| Entry[0]:                                        |
|   ProfileID_SWID = 153419778  (ServiceID 2341)   |
|   ProfileID_ProfileNumber = 0                    |
|   RequestType = 0x01 (ACTIVATE)                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
| RSPS_MsgType = 0x01 (REQ_STATUS_PROF_STATE)      |
| Size_Indicator = 0  (no feedback in this frame)  |
+--------------------------------------------------+</code></pre>

<h4>Step 6: Remote SPM responds</h4>
<pre><code>// Remote SPM at 12.10.2.2 receives the frame:
//   1. Parses PROFILE_REQUEST entries
//   2. Finds matching profile by ServiceID + ProfileNumber
//   3. Activates the local service on its ECU
//   4. Sends back feedback SM Frame:

SM Frame (Rx from 12.10.2.2):
+--------------------------------------------------+
| PMSrcId  = 12.10.2.2                             |
| PMDestId = 12.10.2.1  (our IP)                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
| RSPS_MsgType = 0x01                              |
| Size_Indicator = 1                               |
| Entry[0]:                                        |
|   ProfileID_SWID = 153419778                     |
|   ProfileID_ProfileNumber = 0                    |
|   RequestStatus = 0x01 (OK_ACTIVATION)           |
|   ProfileStatus = 0x02 (ACTIVATED)               |
+--------------------------------------------------+

// Our SPM processes the feedback:
Spm_CheckFeedbackReceivedByRequested(profIdx=0, status=OK_ACTIVATION, state=ACTIVATED)
// Profile 0 FSM: Activating --evActivationComplete--&gt; Activated</code></pre>

<h4>Step 7: All profiles activated</h4>
<pre><code>// Final state of all profiles:
//
// Rear_Closure_2 (Remote)      : ACTIVATED  (via SM Frame to 12.10.2.2)
// HW_Input_Analog (Remote)     : ACTIVATED  (via SM Frame to 12.10.2.3)
// HW_Input_LIN (Local)         : ACTIVATED  (via SrvcMgr on this ECU)
//
// PDU groups enabled for ACT_AND_CONS dependencies
// DID 0xE0DD bitmap updated (bits set for all 3 profiles)
// Activity records updated in DID 0xE0DE (local activation)</code></pre>
</div>

<!-- Example: SM Frame Exchange -->
<h3 id="ex-sm-frame">Example: SM Frame Data Structures</h3>

<p>Here is how the SM Frame is structured in memory, using <strong>real generated data types</strong>:</p>

<pre><code>// The complete SM Frame structure (from Sum_SpmTypes.h):

typedef struct {
    uint32 PMSrcId;           // Source IP address (this ECU)
    uint32 PMDestId;          // Destination IP address (target ECU)

    uint8  PR_MsgType;        // = 0x00 for PROFILE_REQUEST
    ProfileRequestDataType_SvcStruct ProfileRequest;
    //   +-- uint16 Size_Indicator;     // Number of entries
    //   +-- ProfileRequestPayLoad[115] // Max 115 entries per frame
    //        +-- uint32 ProfileID_SWID
    //        +-- uint8  ProfileID_ProfileNumber
    //        +-- uint8  RequestType      // 0x01=ACTIVATE, 0x02=DEACTIVATE

    uint8  RSPS_MsgType;      // = 0x01 for REQ_STATUS_PROF_STATE
    RequestStatusProfileStateDataType_SvcStruct RequestStatusProfileState;
    //   +-- uint16 Size_Indicator;     // Number of entries
    //   +-- RequestStatusProfileStatePayLoad[98] // Max 98 entries
    //        +-- uint32 ProfileID_SWID
    //        +-- uint8  ProfileID_ProfileNumber
    //        +-- uint8  RequestStatus   // See rejection codes
    //        +-- uint8  ProfileStatus   // INACTIVE/ACTIVATING/ACTIVATED/DEACTIVATING
} SPM_dt_Prv;</code></pre>

<p><strong>Building a request (real code from <code>Sum_Spm_SM_Req_EthIf.c</code>):</strong></p>

<pre><code>// Append a profile activation request to the outgoing SM frame:
static void Spm_SoftwMgr_AppendRequest(const uint8 indexPowProf, SPM_dt_Prv *sm_frame)
{
    uint8 idx = (uint8)(SPM_PTR_PROF_REQ_SIZE(sm_frame));

    // Fill in Profile ID (Service+Instance) from config table
    SPM_PTR_PROF_REQ_ID(sm_frame, idx) =
        SpmPowPrf_Cfg_WrpTable[indexPowProf].powPrf_data-&gt;PowPrfID;

    // Fill in Profile Number
    SPM_PTR_PROF_REQ_PROF_NUMBER(sm_frame, idx) =
        SpmPowPrf_Cfg_WrpTable[indexPowProf].powPrf_data-&gt;PowPrfNum;

    // Fill in command: 0x01 = ACTIVATE, 0x02 = DEACTIVATE
    SPM_PTR_PROF_REQ_REQUEST_TYPE(sm_frame, idx) =
        SPM_PrfStsMgr_RAM[indexPowProf].CommandSend;

    SPM_PTR_PROF_REQ_SIZE(sm_frame) += 1u;  // Increment entry count
}</code></pre>

<p><strong>Parsing an incoming SM frame:</strong></p>

<pre><code>// Spm_ReadIncoming_SM_Message() processes received SM frame:
for (i = 0U; i &lt; SPM_REQ_SIZE; i++) {
    // Find which profile matches the ServiceID + ProfileNumber
    indexPowProf = Spm_GetPowProfIndexFromSwIDProfNumber(
        SPM_REQUEST_SIDE_SW_ID(i),
        SPM_REQUEST_SIDE_PROF_NUMBER(i)
    );

    if (SPM_REQ_VAL(i) == 0x01u) {
        // ACTIVATE request from remote
        Spm_Handler_prfReqDispatcherForActivationFromRemote(
            (uint8)indexPowProf, Spm_SM_Rx-&gt;PMSrcId);
    } else {
        // DEACTIVATE request from remote
        Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher(indexPowProf, Spm_SM_Rx-&gt;PMSrcId,
                                  SPM_DEA_REQ, &amp;ActRet);
    }
}

// Process feedback entries:
for (i = 0u; i &lt; SPM_FEEDBACK_SIZE; i++) {
    Spm_CheckFeedbackReceivedByRequested(
        (uint8)indexPowProf,
        SPM_FEEDBACK_SIDE_STATUS_REQ(i),   // OK or REJECTED_*
        SPM_FEEDBACK_SIDE_PROF_STATE(i));   // Current profile state
}</code></pre>

<!-- Example: Wakeup Sequence -->
<h3 id="ex-wakeup-seq">Walkthrough: Wakeup Sequence Execution</h3>

<p>When a remote profile needs activation but the target ECU is <strong>OFF</strong>, SPM executes the configured wakeup sequence. Here is a real sequence from the PGTT:</p>

<div class="card">
<h4>Scenario: Target 12.10.2.2 is OFF, profile Rear_Closure_2 needs activation</h4>

<p>PM detects target device 12.10.2.2 is in state <code>SPM_Off</code>. SM requests <code>Spm_PowerOnDevice(IP=12.10.2.2)</code>. PM looks up PGTT: <code>SpmTrgDvc[0]</code> &rarr; <code>SpmWkUpSeq</code>.</p>

<h4>Wakeup Sequence Steps</h4>
<div class="hflow">
  <div class="flow-step" style="border-color:#0984e3;background:#eef6ff;min-width:140px">
    <strong>Step 1</strong><br>TC10 Wake<small>EthSM_RequestComMode()<br>CmdValue=500</small>
  </div>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;">
    <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
    <div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;margin-top:2px;">250ms delay</div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-step" style="border-color:#e8913a;background:#fff8f0;min-width:140px">
    <strong>Step 2</strong><br>ETH WUF A<small>Set bit 10<br>Unicast send</small>
  </div>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;">
    <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
    <div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--text-light);font-weight:700;margin-top:2px;">0ms (combined)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-step" style="border-color:#00b894;background:#f0fff8;min-width:140px">
    <strong>Step 3</strong><br>CAN WUF A<small>Set bit 11<br>CanIf_Transmit()</small>
  </div>
</div>

<h4>Execution Timeline</h4>
<div class="timeline">
  <div class="tl-event">
    <div class="tl-time">0 ms</div>
    <strong>Step 1:</strong> TC10 wake &mdash; <code>EthSM_RequestComMode(FULL_COMMUNICATION)</code>
    <div class="tl-detail">Start 250ms delay timer...</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tl-event">
    <div class="tl-time">250 ms</div>
    <strong>Step 2:</strong> Set bit 10 in ETH WUF A buffer, send unicast
    <div class="tl-detail">delay=0ms, immediately continue to Step 3</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tl-event">
    <div class="tl-time">250 ms</div>
    <strong>Step 3:</strong> Set bit 11 in CAN WUF A, <code>CanIf_Transmit()</code>
    <div class="tl-detail">delay=0ms &mdash; Steps 2 &amp; 3 combined into single PM cycle</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tl-event">
    <div class="tl-time">~255 ms</div>
    <strong>Wakeup complete.</strong> PM starts monitoring for heartbeat from 12.10.2.2
    <div class="tl-detail">Target transitions: Off &rarr; Initializing (marked as Requested)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tl-event">
    <div class="tl-time">~300 ms</div>
    <strong>First HB received</strong> from 12.10.2.2 (counter=0)
    <div class="tl-detail">Target transitions: Initializing &rarr; On &mdash; ready for SM Frame exchange</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h4>PowerOnDevice retry (if target doesn't respond)</h4>

<p>If no HB is received within <code>SpmTrgDvcTimeOut</code>, the target transitions to <strong>Faulted</strong> and DTC 54802 is reported. The retry FSM kicks in:</p>

<div class="hflow">
  <div class="flow-step gray">No Retry</div>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;">
    <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
    <div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:2px;">Faulted</div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-step remote" style="min-width:110px">PowerOff<small>De-assert all</small></div>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;">
    <div class="hflow-arrow" style="background:var(--accent)"></div>
    <div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;margin-top:2px;">Wait 1s</div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-step local" style="min-width:110px">PowerOn<small>Re-assert all</small></div>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;">
    <div class="hflow-arrow" style="background:var(--accent)"></div>
    <div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;margin-top:2px;">Wait 10s</div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-step hl" style="min-width:110px">Check<small>Recovered?</small></div>
</div>
<p style="text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:-8px;">&#x21bb; Loops until device recovers (state=On) or profiles are deactivated</p>
</div>

<!-- Example: Error Scenarios -->
<h3 id="ex-error-scenarios">Example: Error Handling Scenarios</h3>

<h4>Scenario A: Low Voltage Battery Rejection</h4>

<div class="card">
<pre><code>// Rear_Closure_Output (AppIntfID=11) has priority LOW for Vehicle ON
// Vehicle Energy Optimizer reports current threshold = MEDIUM
//
// Spm_ErrorHandler_LowVoltageBattery() runs periodically:

void Spm_ErrorHandler_LowVoltageBattery(void) {
    for (i = 0; i &lt; 6; i++) {  // SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM = 6
        if (FALSE == Spm_Get_ActivationAvailabilityLowVoltageBatteryPriority(i)) {
            // Profile i's priority is BELOW the threshold
            Spm_SendDeactivationRequestForEachRequester(i, Spm_REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER);
        }
    }
}

// For Rear_Closure_Output (index 1):
//   Priority = LOW (value 1)
//   Threshold = MEDIUM (value 2)
//   1 &lt;= 2 --&gt; TRUE --&gt; activation NOT available
//   Result: REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER (0x15) sent to all requesters
//   Profile deactivated, feedback SM Frame sent with rejection code</code></pre>

<h4>Priority level hierarchy</h4>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Level</th><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>NOT_APPLICABLE</td><td>0</td><td>No priority check (always allowed)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>LOW</td><td>1</td><td>Rejected when threshold &ge; LOW</td></tr>
    <tr><td>MEDIUM</td><td>2</td><td>Rejected when threshold &ge; MEDIUM</td></tr>
    <tr><td>HIGH</td><td>3</td><td>Rejected when threshold &ge; HIGH</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CRITICAL</td><td>4</td><td>Rejected when threshold &ge; CRITICAL (only extreme shortage)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h4>Scenario B: Loss of Communication with a Requester</h4>

<div class="card">
<pre><code>// Remote ECU 12.10.2.3 had activated our local profile HW_Input_LIN
// RequesterList[3] = [{IP=12.10.2.3, ReqType=ACTIVATED}]
//
// But 12.10.2.3 stops sending heartbeats...
// PM detects: DevicePowerState[12.10.2.3] = Faulted (no HB within timeout)
// DTC reported: Sum_Spm_WriteLossofNode(DTC=54803, LOST)

// Spm_LoC_wRequester_Handler() runs in SM cycle:
for each local profile:
    for each requester in requester list:
        deviceState = Spm_GetTrgDvcState(requesterIP)
        if (deviceState == Faulted):
            // Send rejection feedback via SM Frame
            Spm_AppendFeedbackErrorItemToList(
                profIdx=3,
                trgDvcIp=12.10.2.3,
                errorCode=Spm_REJECTED_LOSS_OF_HEARTBEAT,  // 0x18
                swId=2850,
                profileNumber=244
            );
            // Remove requester from list
            // Set SpmStayAwakeTimer (keep alive briefly)

        if (deviceState == Reboot):
            // Similar, but error = Spm_REJECTED_RESET_DETECTED (0x11)

// After LoC cleanup:
// RequesterList[3] = [] (empty)
// FSM detects no requesters:
//   HW_Input_LIN: Activated --evNoRequestActive--&gt; Deactivating --&gt; Inactive
//   Service 2850 deactivated via SrvcMgr</code></pre>
</div>

<h4>Scenario C: Vehicle OFF Timeout</h4>

<div class="card">
<pre><code>// Vehicle power mode changes to OFF
// Spm_ErrorHandler_VehOff() checks each profile:

// Rear_Closure_HW_Output (index 4, LOCAL):
//   SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff = 200ms
//   Countdown timer loaded: 200ms / SM_Periodicity(10ms) = 20 ticks
//
//   Each SM cycle: tick-- (20, 19, 18, ... 1, 0)
//
//   When tick reaches 0 AND a local requester exists:
//     Spm_prv_prfReqDispatcher(index=4, IP=0, SPM_DEA_REQ)
//     Profile is deactivated (battery conservation)

// Rear_Closure_HW_Input_LIN (index 3, LOCAL):
//   SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff = 10ms = 1 tick
//   Deactivated after just 1 SM cycle (fastest timeout)

// Rear_Closure_2 (index 0, REMOTE):
//   SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff = 100ms = 10 ticks
//   After 10 cycles, deactivation request sent via SM Frame

// Rear_Closure_Output (index 1, REMOTE):
//   SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff = 0ms
//   0 means: no timeout, profile stays active indefinitely in VehOff
//   (Used for critical services that must survive power-off)</code></pre>
</div>

<h4>Scenario D: Rejection Code Retry Behavior</h4>

<div class="card">
<p>When a remote SPM rejects our activation request, the <strong>rejection code determines the retry strategy</strong>:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Rejection Code</th><th>Value</th><th>Retry</th><th>Action</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>REJECTED_PROFILE_UNKNOWN</code></td><td>0x12</td><td>Slow</td><td>Profile not configured on remote; retry at slow rate</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>REJECTED_LACK_OF_PERMISSION</code></td><td>0x13</td><td>Slow</td><td>Not authorized; retry hoping config changes</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER</code></td><td>0x15</td><td>Fast</td><td>Trigger LV Optimizer Check + retry at fast rate</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>REJECTED_PROFILE_BLOCKED</code></td><td>0x17</td><td>Fast</td><td>Learning session in progress; retry at fast rate</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>REJECTED_LOSS_OF_HEARTBEAT</code></td><td>0x18</td><td>Slow</td><td>Remote lost our HB; wait for recovery</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>REJECTED_RESET_DETECTED</code></td><td>0x11</td><td>Slow</td><td>Remote detected our reboot; wait for re-sync</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>REJECTED_REQUEST_INVALID</code></td><td>0x10</td><td>Slow</td><td>Malformed request; retry at slow rate</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>REQUEST_ACCEPTED</code></td><td>0xFF</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Success! No retry needed</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<pre><code>// In Spm_RemotePowerProfile_FSM:
// Profile stays in "Activating" state and retries:
//
//   Fast retry: SpmActDeactRetryPeriodicity (configurable, e.g., 100ms)
//   Slow retry: Longer interval for persistent errors
//
// The FSM does NOT give up -- it keeps retrying until:
//   1. Remote responds with REQUEST_ACCEPTED, or
//   2. The profile is deactivated by the local SWC, or
//   3. Loss-of-communication forces requester removal</code></pre>
</div>

<hr>

<h2 id="section-6">6. Module Architecture (Internal Design)</h2>

<h3>Generated Modules</h3>

<p>All modules below are generated from Xpand templates. <strong>Never edit the generated .c/.h files directly</strong> &mdash; edit the <code>.xpt</code> template instead.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Module</th><th>Source Files</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>PwrMgr</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_PwrMgr.c/.h</code></td><td>Power Manager main function: HB Tx/Rx, wakeup execution, device state evaluation</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>SoftwMgr</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_SoftwMgr.c/.h</code></td><td>Software Manager main function: SM frame Tx/Rx, profile FSM, request dispatching</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>PowerProfileStateMachine</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_PowerProfileStateMachine.c/.h</code></td><td>Per-profile FSM (Inactive/Activating/Activated/Deactivating) for local and remote profiles</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>DevicePowerState</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_DevicePowerState.c/.h</code></td><td>Device power state FSM (Off/Initializing/On/Faulted/Reboot/PendingShutdown)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>HeartBeat_Mgr</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_HeartBeat_Mgr.c/.h</code></td><td>HB counter management, burst/steady-state timing</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>WakeUp</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_WakeUp.c/.h</code></td><td>Wakeup sequence execution, WUF Tx/Rx, timing</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>PowerOnDevice</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_PowerOnDevice.c/.h</code></td><td>PowerOn/Off device sequences, retry logic</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>ErrorHandler</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_ErrorHandler.c/.h</code></td><td>Error detection: LoC, LowVoltage, VehOff, conflicting requests</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Request_Queue</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_Request_Queue.c/.h</code></td><td>Internal request queue for profile activation/deactivation</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>RequesterLst</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_RequesterLst.c/.h</code></td><td>Per-profile requester list management</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Cbk</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_Cbk.c/.h</code></td><td>Callback implementations for NvM, Com, BswM notifications, CAN Rx/Tx</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Services</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_Services.c/.h</code></td><td>C/S API implementations: ActivateProfile, DeactivateProfile, GetProfileState, etc.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Diagnostic</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_Diagnostic.c/.h</code></td><td>DID read services: E0DD, E0DE, E0DF</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>MetaData</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_MetaData.c/.h</code></td><td>Metadata handling for SOME/IP frames (source IP)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>SrvcMgrIf</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_SrvcMgrIf.c/.h</code></td><td>Interface to Service Manager</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>SM_Req_EthIf</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_SM_Req_EthIf.c/.h</code></td><td>SM frame builder and Ethernet communication</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Cfg/PBCfg</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_Cfg.c/.h</code>, <code>Sum_Spm_PBCfg.c/.h</code></td><td>Compile-time and post-build configuration data</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>VEO</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_Interaction_VehicleEnergyOptimizer.c/.h</code></td><td>Vehicle Energy Optimizer (low voltage priority) interaction</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>VariantManagement</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_VariantManagement.c/.h</code></td><td>Branded/unbranded variant handling</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>WufRollingBuffer</strong></td><td><code>Sum_Spm_WufRollingBuffer.c/.h</code></td><td>Rolling buffer for received wakeup frames</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Hand-Written Modules</h3>

<p>Located in <code>20_Implementation/</code>:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>File</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>src/Sum_Spm_CanIfDispatchUL.c</code></td><td>CAN interface dispatch &mdash; routes CAN Tx confirmation and Rx indication to SPM</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>src/Sum_Spm_CommErrHndlr.c</code></td><td>Communication error handler for CAN WUF transmission errors</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>api/Sum_Spm_Integration.h</code></td><td>Integration header &mdash; defines <code>SPM_NUMBER_ITEM_IN_SM_FRAME</code> and project-specific macros</td></tr>
