    <tr><td><code>api/Cdd.h</code></td><td>CDD header dummy required for BSW code generation</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Power Profile FSM Events</h3>

<pre><code>enum SpmPowerProfileStateMachineEventsCode {
    Spm_PrfMgr_evDeactivationRequest = 0,   // Deactivation requested
    Spm_PrfMgr_evActivationComplete  = 1,   // Service activation succeeded
    Spm_PrfMgr_evNoRequestActive     = 2,   // No more active requesters
    Spm_PrfMgr_evActivationRequest   = 3,   // Activation requested
    Spm_PrfMgr_evDeactivationComplete= 4,   // Service deactivation succeeded
    Spm_PrfMgr_evActivationFailed    = 5,   // Service activation failed
    Spm_PrfMgr_evDeactivationFailed  = 6    // Service deactivation failed
};</code></pre>

<h3>Power Profile FSM State Diagram</h3>

<div class="svg-wrap">
<svg viewBox="0 0 620 320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:Segoe UI,sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs>
    <marker id="pa" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#1a3a5c"/></marker>
    <marker id="pa-g" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#00b894"/></marker>
    <marker id="pa-o" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#e8913a"/></marker>
    <marker id="pa-r" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#d63031"/></marker>
  </defs>

  <!-- States -->
  <rect x="30" y="100" width="130" height="55" rx="27" fill="#f8f9fa" stroke="#636e72" stroke-width="3"/>
  <text x="95" y="133" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="14" fill="#636e72">Inactive</text>

  <rect x="250" y="30" width="130" height="55" rx="27" fill="#eef6ff" stroke="#0984e3" stroke-width="3"/>
  <text x="315" y="63" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="14" fill="#0984e3">Activating</text>

  <rect x="460" y="100" width="130" height="55" rx="27" fill="#e6fff7" stroke="#00b894" stroke-width="3"/>
  <text x="525" y="133" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="14" fill="#00b894">Activated</text>

  <rect x="250" y="200" width="130" height="55" rx="27" fill="#fff8f0" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="3"/>
  <text x="315" y="233" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="14" fill="#e8913a">Deactivating</text>

  <!-- Inactive -> Activating -->
  <path d="M150,105 Q200,50 250,55" fill="none" stroke="#0984e3" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#pa)"/>
  <text x="160" y="55" font-size="11" fill="#0984e3" font-weight="600">evActivationRequest</text>

  <!-- Activating -> Activated -->
  <path d="M380,60 Q430,60 460,105" fill="none" stroke="#00b894" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#pa-g)"/>
  <text x="400" y="62" font-size="11" fill="#00b894" font-weight="600">evActivationComplete</text>

  <!-- Activated -> Deactivating -->
  <path d="M520,155 Q520,230 380,230" fill="none" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#pa-o)"/>
  <text x="420" y="200" font-size="11" fill="#e8913a" font-weight="600">evDeactivationRequest</text>

  <!-- Deactivating -> Inactive -->
  <path d="M250,230 Q170,230 100,155" fill="none" stroke="#636e72" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#pa)"/>
  <text x="120" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#636e72" font-weight="600">evDeactivationComplete</text>

  <!-- Self-loop: Activating retries -->
  <path d="M280,30 Q280,2 340,2 Q370,2 360,30" fill="none" stroke="#d63031" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-dasharray="4,3" marker-end="url(#pa-r)"/>
  <text x="280" y="-2" font-size="10" fill="#d63031" font-weight="600">evActivationFailed (retries)</text>

  <!-- Self-loop: Deactivating retries -->
  <path d="M280,255 Q280,280 340,280 Q370,280 360,255" fill="none" stroke="#d63031" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-dasharray="4,3" marker-end="url(#pa-r)"/>
  <text x="270" y="298" font-size="10" fill="#d63031" font-weight="600">evDeactivationFailed (retries)</text>

  <!-- evNoRequestActive: Activating -> Deactivating -->
  <line x1="315" y1="85" x2="315" y2="200" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,3" marker-end="url(#pa-o)"/>
  <text x="322" y="150" font-size="10" fill="#e8913a">evNoRequestActive</text>
</svg>
</div>

<blockquote>
  <p><strong>Retry behavior:</strong> When an activation is rejected by a remote SPM, the profile FSM stays in <code>Activating</code> and retries with tiered periodicity. The retry rate (fast vs slow) depends on the rejection reason &mdash; e.g., <code>REJECTED_LOSS_OF_HEARTBEAT</code> uses slow retry, while <code>REJECTED_LACK_OF_POWER</code> triggers an LV Optimizer Check profile activation.</p>
</blockquote>

<h3>Key Implementation Constants (Current Config)</h3>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Constant</th><th>Value</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM</code></td><td>6</td><td>Number of configured power profiles</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SUM_SPM_NUMBER_OF_NET_CONF</code></td><td>1</td><td>Number of network configurations</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SUM_SPM_NUMBER_OF_VARIANTS</code></td><td>2</td><td>Number of variants (branded/unbranded)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SPM_REQER_LST_SIZE</code></td><td>configurable</td><td>Requester list size per profile</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Request Queue Max</td><td>12</td><td>2 x number of profiles (activate + deactivate)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>HB Burst Count</td><td>3</td><td>Number of initial rapid heartbeat transmissions</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Shutdown HB Range</td><td>&ge; 0xFFFFFF00</td><td>HeartbeatCounter values indicating shutdown pending</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Execution Flow</h3>

<h4>Every 5ms (<code>RE_SPM_PowerManager_MainFunction</code>)</h4>
<ol>
  <li>Read PermitExecution from SUSD</li>
  <li>Poll HB Rx queue &mdash; update device power states</li>
  <li>Execute wakeup sequences (if any pending)</li>
  <li>Transmit heartbeat (burst or steady-state)</li>
  <li>Handle wakeup frame Tx/Rx timing</li>
  <li>Write Loss-of-Node indication to SSFM</li>
</ol>

<h4>Every SM period (configurable, default 1000ms, <code>RE_SPM_SoftMgr_MainFunction</code>)</h4>
<ol>
  <li>Check PermitExecution mask and initialization state</li>
  <li>Read SM frame Rx queue &mdash; dispatch remote requests</li>
  <li>Process local activation/deactivation queue</li>
  <li>Execute profile FSM for each local profile</li>
  <li>Execute profile FSM for each remote profile</li>
  <li>Handle requester list cleanup</li>
  <li>Handle error conditions (LoC, LowVoltage, VehOff)</li>
  <li>Populate and send SM frames (requests + status feedback)</li>
  <li>Send service activation notification to SSFM</li>
  <li>Update DID 0xE0D7 to SUSD</li>
  <li>Update activity timers for DID 0xE0DE/0xE0DF</li>
</ol>

<hr>

<!-- Section 7 -->
<h2 id="section-7">7. Code Generation System</h2>

<h3>Why Code Generation?</h3>

<p>SPM's code is <strong>configuration-driven</strong>: the number of profiles, target devices, VLANs, wakeup sequences, DIDs, etc. all vary per project. Rather than runtime configuration with arrays of variable size, SPM generates <strong>optimized, statically-sized C code</strong> from AUTOSAR ECUC configuration.</p>

<h3>How It Works</h3>

<div class="hflow">
  <div class="flow-step" style="border-color:#6c5ce7;background:#f3f0ff;min-width:150px">
    <strong>ECUC Config</strong><br><code style="font-size:11px">.arxml</code>
    <small>30_Generation/<br>ecu_config/sum/</small>
  </div>
  <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step hl" style="min-width:150px">
    <strong>Xpand Templates</strong><br><code style="font-size:11px">.xpt / .ext</code>
    <small>20_Implementation/<br>scripts/templates/</small>
  </div>
  <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
  <div class="flow-step local" style="min-width:150px">
    <strong>Generated C Code</strong><br><code style="font-size:11px">.c / .h</code>
    <small>30_Generation/<br>src/sum/</small>
  </div>
</div>

<p><strong>Toolchain:</strong></p>
<ol>
  <li><code>Spm_EcucParamDef.arxml</code> defines the parameter schema (what can be configured)</li>
  <li>ECUC values <code>.arxml</code> files contain the actual configuration</li>
  <li><code>Sum_Spm_Generate.oaw</code> (OpenArchitectureWare) orchestrates generation</li>
  <li><code>Sum_Spm_Validate.oaw</code> runs validation checks (<code>Sum_Spm.chk</code>)</li>
  <li>46 <code>.xpt</code> template files produce ~41 C/H source files + 1 CDD arxml</li>
</ol>

<p><strong>Helper extensions:</strong> <code>Spm_Utils.ext</code> provides utility functions used across templates (e.g., IP address lookups, VLAN matching, profile enumeration).</p>

<h3>Template Encoding Warning</h3>

<p><code>.xpt</code> and <code>.ext</code> files are <strong>ISO-8859-1 encoded</strong>. When editing:</p>

<pre><code># Convert to UTF-8 before editing
iconv -f ISO-8859-1 -t UTF-8 &lt; template.xpt &gt; template_utf8.xpt

# Edit template_utf8.xpt

# Convert back before committing
iconv -f UTF-8 -t ISO-8859-1 &lt; template_utf8.xpt &gt; template.xpt</code></pre>

<h3>Paramdef from YAML (Design-Driven)</h3>

<p>The parameter definition (<code>Spm_EcucParamDef.arxml</code>) is itself <strong>generated</strong> from YAML:</p>

<div class="hflow">
  <div class="flow-step" style="border-color:#6c5ce7;background:#f3f0ff;min-width:160px">
    <strong>YAML Config</strong><br><code style="font-size:11px">Spm_paramConf.yaml</code>
    <small>design_driven/</small>
  </div>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;">
    <div class="hflow-arrow"></div>
    <div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;margin-top:2px;">generate_paramdef.py</div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-step local" style="min-width:160px">
    <strong>ParamDef ARXML</strong><br><code style="font-size:11px">Spm_EcucParamDef.arxml</code>
    <small>20_Implementation/<br>scripts/paramdef/</small>
  </div>
</div>

<p><strong>Never edit <code>Spm_EcucParamDef.arxml</code> directly</strong> &mdash; edit <code>Spm_paramConf.yaml</code> instead.</p>

<h3 id="yaml-deep-dive">YAML Configuration Deep-Dive &mdash; <code>parameters_structure.yaml</code></h3>

<p>The YAML file (<code>design_driven/Spm_paramConf.yaml</code>) is the <strong>single source of truth</strong> for every AUTOSAR ECUC parameter the SPM module exposes. It defines the schema &mdash; parameter names, types, multiplicities, ranges, and defaults &mdash; that project integrators fill in to configure an SPM instance on a specific ECU.</p>

<details open>
<summary><strong>7.1 &nbsp; YAML Structure Overview</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<p>The YAML is organized into hierarchical containers that mirror the AUTOSAR ECUC container tree:</p>

<pre><code class="yaml">@startyaml
SpmConfigSet:
SpmGeneral:                  # ECU-level timing, masks, helper functions
  - SpmSMMainFuncPeriodicity
  - SpmPMMainFuncPeriodicity
  - SpmBurstPhsPeriodicity
  - SpmPermitExecutionMask
  - SpmWkUpHelperFunction
SpmETHWkUpFrmRef:            # Ethernet wake-up frame PDU references
SpmCANWkUpFrmRef:            # CAN wake-up frame Tx/Rx PDU references
SpmVLANCom:                  # VLAN identifiers for multi-VLAN ECUs
SpmPowPrf:                   # Power Profile definitions (core entity)
  +-- SpmProfileSwDep:       #   Software dependencies between profiles
SpmPgttEntries:              # Power Graph Traversal Table
  +-- SpmTrgDvc:             #   Target Devices (remote ECUs to wake)
  |    +-- SpmTrgDvcHndlngInfo  # Wake-up frame bit assignment
  +-- SpmWkngDvc:            #   Waking Device (this ECU)
  |    +-- SpmTrgDvcInfo     #   Links targets to wake-up sequences
  +-- SpmWkUpSeq:            #   Wake-up Sequences
       +-- SpmWkUpStep       #   Individual steps (TC10, ETH, CAN, GPIO)
@endyaml</code></pre>

<svg viewBox="0 0 620 340" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
