</div>
</details>

<!-- 7.2 SpmGeneral -->
<details>
<summary><strong>7.2 &nbsp; SpmGeneral &mdash; ECU-Level Settings</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<p>Controls timing, scheduling, and system-wide masks that affect all SPM features.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th><th>Feature Impact</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmSMMainFuncPeriodicity</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>10.0 ms</td><td>Software Manager main function scheduling period</td><td>Controls how fast SM frame processing, profile FSM transitions, and DID updates execute. Lower = more responsive but higher CPU load.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmPMMainFuncPeriodicity</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>5.0 ms</td><td>Power Manager main function scheduling period</td><td>Controls heartbeat Tx/Rx timing and wake-up sequence step execution. Must be &le; heartbeat burst period.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmBurstPhsPeriodicity</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>5 ms</td><td>Burst-phase heartbeat period (first 3 transmissions)</td><td>After PowerOnDevice, 3 rapid heartbeats are sent at this rate before switching to steady-state (1000 ms). Faster = quicker remote detection.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmPermitExecutionMask</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>0xFE</td><td>1-byte wake-up source mask</td><td>Bits that are "don't care" for SPM execution permission. If <code>(WakeUpReason &amp; ~Mask) != 0</code>, SPM is allowed to execute. Mask <code>0xFE</code> means only bit 0 matters.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmWkUpHelperFunction</code></td><td>STRING</td><td><em>(optional)</em></td><td>Name of project-specific GPIO wake-up function</td><td>When set, generates <code>#include "Sum_Spm_WakeUpHelper.h"</code> and calls this function for <code>SEND_BOARD_LV_WKUP_GPIO</code> steps. Required if any wake-up sequence uses GPIO commands.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>Example: How <code>SpmPermitExecutionMask</code> gates SPM startup</h4>
<pre><code class="yaml"># YAML definition
- Name: SpmPermitExecutionMask
  Type: INTEGER
  Min: 0
  Max: 255
  Default: 254    # 0xFE = binary 1111_1110</code></pre>
<pre><code class="c">// Generated in Sum_Spm_Cfg.h:
#define SPM_PERMIT_EXEC_MASK  (0xFEu)

// Runtime check in SPM init:
if ((wakeUpReason & ~SPM_PERMIT_EXEC_MASK) != 0u) {
    // SPM is permitted to execute &rarr; initialize profiles, start heartbeat
} else {
    // SPM stays dormant &rarr; no profiles activated, no power management
}</code></pre>
<p><strong>Impact:</strong> Setting mask to <code>0xFF</code> would disable SPM entirely (no wake-up source can trigger it). Setting to <code>0x00</code> means <em>any</em> wake-up source permits SPM.</p>

</div>
</details>

<!-- 7.3 SpmPowPrf -->
<details>
<summary><strong>7.3 &nbsp; SpmPowPrf &mdash; Power Profile Configuration</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<p>The <strong>Power Profile</strong> is the central entity in SPM. Each profile represents a service (e.g., "Remote Climate Control", "OTA Update", "Telematics Streaming") that can be activated/deactivated. The YAML defines the schema; each project creates one <code>SpmPowPrf</code> instance per service.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Feature Impact</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmSrvcAndInstID</code></td><td>INTEGER (32-bit)</td><td>Upper 16 bits = Service ID, lower 16 bits = Instance ID</td><td>Globally unique key used in SM frame communication between ECUs. Must match the SOME/IP service discovery definition.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmProfNumber</code></td><td>INTEGER (0-255)</td><td>Profile index within the service</td><td>Combined with SrvcAndInstID to sort and index profiles. Determines array position in <code>Spm_Prf_Cfg[]</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmProfileIsLocal</code></td><td>BOOLEAN</td><td>TRUE = local SW entity, FALSE = remote service</td><td><strong>Critical branch:</strong> Local profiles use C/S activation API. Remote profiles use SM frames + PowerOnDevice wake-up sequences.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmLocActivationAllowed</code></td><td>BOOLEAN</td><td>Accept local <code>SPM_ActivateProfile</code> requests?</td><td>When FALSE, the profile can only be activated by remote SM frames. Prevents unauthorized local activation of server-only profiles.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmApplIntfID</code></td><td>INTEGER (0-65535)</td><td>Application Interface ID for C/S calls</td><td>The value passed in <code>SPM_ActivateProfile(applIntfID)</code> to identify which profile to activate. Each local profile must have a unique ID.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmProfBitMapIndex</code></td><td>INTEGER (0-511)</td><td>Bit position in DID 0xE0DD bitmap</td><td>Controls which bit in the diagnostic activation status DID represents this profile. Used by tester tools to read profile states.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmVehDefActPriorON</code></td><td>ENUM</td><td>Low-voltage priority when vehicle is ON</td><td>Energy optimizer can deactivate profiles whose priority &lt; current threshold. <code>SPM_PRF_AP_NOTAPP</code> = exempt from low-voltage constraints.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmVehDefActPriorOFF</code></td><td>ENUM</td><td>Low-voltage priority when vehicle is OFF</td><td>Same logic but for vehicle-OFF state. Typically lower priority since battery is more constrained.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff</code></td><td>INTEGER (seconds)</td><td>Max time profile stays active when vehicle OFF</td><td>Safety net: prevents indefinite battery drain. After timeout, profile is force-deactivated.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmComIPduGroupEvnt_Tx/Rx</code></td><td>REFERENCE</td><td>COM I-PDU Groups to enable/disable</td><td>When profile activates, these PDU groups are enabled via BswM &rarr; Com_IpduGroupControl. When profile deactivates, they are disabled. This is how SPM controls network communication per-service.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>Priority Enumeration Values</h4>
<pre><code class="yaml">Range:
  - SPM_PRF_AP_NOTAPP       # Not applicable (exempt from low-voltage)
  - SPM_PRF_AP_LOW          # Lowest priority - first to be cut
  - SPM_PRF_AP_MEDIUM_LOW
  - SPM_PRF_AP_MEDIUM
  - SPM_PRF_AP_MEDIUM_HIGH
  - SPM_PRF_AP_HIGH
  - SPM_PRF_AP_CRITICAL     # Safety-critical - last to be cut
  - SPM_PRF_AP_EMERGENCY
  - SPM_PRF_AP_ACCESS       # Highest - vehicle access (unlock/lock)</code></pre>

<h4>Concrete Example: Remote Climate Control Profile</h4>
<pre><code class="yaml"># Project YAML (filled by integrator based on YAML schema):
SpmPowPrf:
  - SpmSrvcAndInstID:   0x01230001   # Service 0x0123, Instance 0x0001
    SpmProfNumber:       0
    SpmProfileIsLocal:   False         # Remote service on HVAC ECU
    SpmLocActivationAllowed: False     # Cannot be activated locally
    SpmApplIntfID:       -             # Not used (remote)
    SpmProfBitMapIndex:  3             # Bit 3 in DID 0xE0DD
    SpmVehDefActPriorON: SPM_PRF_AP_MEDIUM
    SpmVehDefActPriorOFF: SPM_PRF_AP_LOW
    SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff: 1800  # 30 min max when vehicle OFF
    SpmComIPduGroupEvnt_Tx:
      - ComIPduGroup_HVAC_Tx          # Enable HVAC Tx when activated
    SpmComIPduGroupEvnt_Rx:
      - ComIPduGroup_HVAC_Rx          # Enable HVAC Rx when activated</code></pre>

<pre><code class="c">// Generated in Sum_Spm_Cfg.c:
const SpmConfPowPrf Spm_Prf_Cfg[SPM_NUM_OF_PROFILES] = {
    [0] = {
        .srvcInstId     = 0x01230001u,
        .profNumber     = 0u,
        .isLocal        = FALSE,
        .locActAllowed  = FALSE,
        .bitMapIndex    = 3u,
        .priorON        = SPM_MEDIUM,
        .priorOFF       = SPM_LOW,
        .timeoutVehOff  = 1800u,
        .pduGrpTx       = &amp;Spm_Rte_SwitchPduGroup_HVAC_tx_refs[0],
        .pduGrpRx       = &amp;Spm_Rte_SwitchPduGroup_HVAC_rx_refs[0],
    },
    // ...
};</code></pre>

<p><strong>Runtime impact:</strong> When a remote ECU sends an SM frame requesting service 0x0123 instance 0x0001, SPM:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Looks up <code>Spm_Prf_Cfg[0]</code> by matching <code>srvcInstId</code></li>
  <li>Checks <code>priorON = SPM_MEDIUM</code> against energy optimizer threshold</li>
  <li>If allowed, transitions the profile FSM to <strong>Activating</strong></li>
  <li>Enables <code>ComIPduGroup_HVAC_Tx</code> and <code>ComIPduGroup_HVAC_Rx</code> via BswM</li>
  <li>Executes the PowerOnDevice wake-up sequence for the HVAC ECU (if needed)</li>
  <li>Once HVAC ECU heartbeat is confirmed, transitions to <strong>Activated</strong></li>
  <li>Sets bit 3 in DID 0xE0DD for diagnostic visibility</li>
</ol>

</div>
</details>

<!-- 7.4 SpmProfileSwDep -->
<details>
<summary><strong>7.4 &nbsp; SpmProfileSwDep &mdash; Profile Dependencies</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<p>A profile can depend on other profiles. Dependencies define <strong>activation chains</strong>: when a root profile is activated, all its dependencies are activated first.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmProfDepType</code></td><td>ENUM</td><td><code>SPM_PRF_DEP_ACT_AND_CONS</code> = activate + enable PDU groups<br><code>SPM_PRF_ACTIVATED</code> = activate only (no PDU groups)<br><code>SPM_PRF_CONSUMED</code> = enable PDU groups only (no activation)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmProfRef</code></td><td>REFERENCE</td><td>Reference to the dependent <code>SpmPowPrf</code> instance</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>Example: OTA Update depends on Telematics Gateway</h4>
<pre><code class="yaml">SpmPowPrf:
  - Name: OTA_Update_Profile
    SpmSrvcAndInstID: 0x04560001
    SpmProfileIsLocal: True
    SpmProfileSwDep:
      - SpmProfDepType: SPM_PRF_DEP_ACT_AND_CONS
        SpmProfRef: Telematics_GW_Profile   # Must wake + enable comms
      - SpmProfDepType: SPM_PRF_CONSUMED
        SpmProfRef: Diag_Server_Profile     # Only need its PDU groups</code></pre>

<pre><code class="c">// Generated dependency list:
const SpmProfDep Spm_DeptList_OTA_Update[] = {
    { .depType = SPM_PRF_DEP_ACT_AND_CONS, .depPrfIdx = 2 },  // Telematics
    { .depType = SPM_PRF_CONSUMED,          .depPrfIdx = 5 },  // Diag Server
};</code></pre>

<p><strong>Runtime:</strong> Activating OTA_Update triggers: (1) PowerOnDevice for Telematics GW ECU + enable its PDU groups, (2) enable Diag Server PDU groups (no wake-up needed since it's already local). OTA_Update only transitions to Activated once all dependencies are satisfied.</p>

</div>
</details>

<!-- 7.5 SpmTrgDvc + SpmWkUpSeq -->
<details>
<summary><strong>7.5 &nbsp; SpmTrgDvc + SpmWkUpSeq &mdash; Target Devices &amp; Wake-Up Sequences</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<p>The <strong>Power Graph Traversal Table (PGTT)</strong> defines the network topology: which remote ECUs (target devices) exist, how to wake them up, and how to monitor them.</p>

<h4>SpmTrgDvc &mdash; Target Device Parameters</h4>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Feature Impact</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmTrgDvcID</code></td><td>STRING (1..Inf)</td><td>IP addresses of the target device</td><td>Converted to uint32 and sorted for binary search in <code>Spm_GetIndexTrgDvcFromIP()</code>. Multiple IPs = multi-homed device.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmTrgDvcDtcBaseID</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>DTC base ID for LossOfNode diagnostics</td><td>When heartbeat timeout expires, SPM reports <code>DtcBaseID + offset</code> to DEM. Visible in diagnostic tester as "Node X lost communication".</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmTrgDvcDtcTimeOut</code></td><td>INTEGER (ms)</td><td>Heartbeat timeout</td><td>If no heartbeat received within this window, target is declared lost. Triggers LossOfNode DTC + profile deactivation cascade.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmTrgDvcDiagAddr</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>UDS diagnostic address</td><td>Used for diagnostic routing when reporting target device faults.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>SpmTrgDvcHndlngInfo &mdash; Wake-Up Frame Bit Assignment (Intermediate Nodes Only)</h4>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmTrgAssocWkUpFrm</code></td><td>ENUM</td><td>Which CAN wake-up frame (A or B) carries this target's bit</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmTrgAssocWkupBit</code></td><td>INTEGER (0-63)</td><td>Bit position within the wake-up frame</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>SpmWkUpSeq / SpmWkUpStep &mdash; Wake-Up Sequence Steps</h4>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmStepID</code></td><td>INTEGER (1-255)</td><td>Execution order (sorted ascending)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmCommandType</code></td><td>ENUM</td><td><code>SEND_TC10_SWTCH_1/2</code> &mdash; Ethernet TC10 sleep/wake<br><code>SEND_ETH_WKUP_FRM_A/B</code> &mdash; Ethernet wake-up frame<br><code>SEND_CAN_WKUP_FRM_A/B</code> &mdash; CAN wake-up frame<br><code>SEND_BOARD_LV_WKUP_GPIO</code> &mdash; Board-level GPIO toggle</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmCommandValue</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Port number (TC10), bit position (WUF), or GPIO number</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmSeqStepDly</code></td><td>INTEGER (ms)</td><td>Delay after this step before executing next</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>Full Example: Waking Up a Camera ECU via Ethernet Switch</h4>
<pre><code class="yaml"># Target Device: Front Camera ECU
SpmTrgDvc:
  - SpmTrgDvcID: ["192.168.1.50"]
    SpmTrgDvcDtcBaseID: 0x1234
    SpmTrgDvcDtcTimeOut: 3000        # 3 seconds heartbeat timeout
    SpmTrgDvcDiagAddr: 0x30

# Wake-up Sequence: TC10 switch port wake + ETH wake-up frame
SpmWkUpSeq:
  - Name: WkUpSeq_FrontCamera
    SpmWkUpStep:
      - SpmStepID: 1
        SpmCommandType: SEND_TC10_SWTCH_1   # Wake Ethernet switch port
        SpmCommandValue: 3                    # Port 3
        SpmSeqStepDly: 50                     # Wait 50ms for link up

      - SpmStepID: 2
        SpmCommandType: SEND_ETH_WKUP_FRM_A  # Send ETH wake-up frame A
        SpmCommandValue: 5                    # Bit 5 = Front Camera
        SpmSeqStepDly: 100                    # Wait 100ms for boot

      - SpmStepID: 3
        SpmCommandType: SEND_ETH_WKUP_FRM_A  # Repeat for reliability
        SpmCommandValue: 5
        SpmSeqStepDly: 0                      # No delay after last step

# Link target to sequence:
SpmTrgDvcInfo:
  - SpmTrgDvcRef: TrgDvc_FrontCamera
    SpmWkUpSeqRef: WkUpSeq_FrontCamera</code></pre>

<svg viewBox="0 0 620 310" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs><marker id="wk_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker></defs>
