</div>
</details>

<!-- 7.6 SpmVLANCom -->
<details>
<summary><strong>7.6 &nbsp; SpmVLANCom + SpmCANWkUpFrmRef &mdash; Network Communication</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<h4>SpmVLANCom &mdash; VLAN Configuration</h4>
<p>For ECUs on multiple VLANs, each <code>SpmVLANCom</code> instance defines a VLAN identifier. SPM generates per-VLAN communication handlers:</p>

<pre><code class="yaml"># YAML schema:
SpmVLANCom:
  - Name: SpmVLANId
    Type: INTEGER
    Min: 0
    Max: 255</code></pre>

<pre><code class="c">// Generated per-VLAN handlers in Sum_Spm_Cfg.c:
void Spm_VLAN10_PwrMgrHeartbeatHandleCom(void);   // HB on VLAN 10
void Spm_VLAN10_PwrMgrWakeupHandleCom(void);      // WUF on VLAN 10
void Spm_VLAN10_SwMgrInfoHandleCom(void);          // SM frames on VLAN 10

void Spm_VLAN20_PwrMgrHeartbeatHandleCom(void);   // HB on VLAN 20
// ... etc.

// Top-level dispatcher:
void Spm_HandleVLANCommunication(uint8 vlanId) {
    switch (vlanId) {
        case 10: Spm_VLAN10_PwrMgrHeartbeatHandleCom(); break;
        case 20: Spm_VLAN20_PwrMgrHeartbeatHandleCom(); break;
    }
}</code></pre>

<h4>SpmCANWkUpFrmRef &mdash; CAN Wake-Up Frame References</h4>
<p>Only relevant for <strong>Intermediate nodes</strong> (<code>SpmNodeType = SPM_NODE_INTERMEDIATE</code>) that relay wake-up requests via CAN.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Multiplicity</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmCANWkUpFrmTxRef</code></td><td>0..2</td><td>CanIf Tx PDU references for CAN WUF A/B. Resolved by CanId (339=A, 355=B, 371=C) to generate <code>Spm_CanIf_Tx_WakeUpFrame_A/B/C</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmCANWkUpFrmRxRef</code></td><td>0..Inf</td><td>CanIf Rx PDU references for receiving CAN WUFs. Generates <code>Spm_CanIf_Rx[]</code> array.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p><strong>Validation rule:</strong> The <code>Sum_Spm.chk</code> validator ensures that Edge nodes cannot use CAN wake-up commands, and GPIO commands require <code>SpmWkUpHelperFunction</code> to be configured.</p>

</div>
</details>

<!-- 7.7 SpmWkngDvc -->
<details>
<summary><strong>7.7 &nbsp; SpmWkngDvc &mdash; Local Node Identity</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<p>Defines the local ECU's role in the power graph.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Feature Impact</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>SpmNodeType</code></td><td>ENUM</td><td><code>SPM_NODE_EDGE</code> or <code>SPM_NODE_INTERMEDIATE</code></td><td><strong>Major code-generation branch.</strong> Intermediate nodes get CAN WUF support, CAN Tx/Rx structures, relay logic, and GPIO helper inclusion. Edge nodes only get ETH/TC10 support.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmSrcIp</code></td><td>STRING (1..Inf)</td><td>Source IP addresses of this ECU</td><td>Used in heartbeat, wake-up, and SM frame transmission. Converted to uint32 via <code>Spm_ComputeIpAddr()</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmDstIp</code></td><td>STRING (1..Inf)</td><td>Destination IPs for communication</td><td>Multicast or unicast addresses for SPM protocol frames.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SpmIntermediateDstAddrs</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Relay destination addresses</td><td>Only for intermediate nodes relaying wake-up requests to other network segments.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h4>Edge vs Intermediate Node Comparison</h4>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Edge Node</th><th>Intermediate Node</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Ethernet TC10 wake-up</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Ethernet WUF Tx/Rx</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CAN WUF Tx/Rx</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GPIO wake-up</td><td>No</td><td>Yes (if helper set)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Wake-up relay to sub-networks</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CAN WUF bit monitoring</td><td>No</td><td>Yes (SpmTrgDvcHndlngInfo)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

</div>
</details>

<!-- 7.8 Complete Example -->
<details>
<summary><strong>7.8 &nbsp; Complete Example: YAML &rarr; Generated Code &rarr; Runtime Behavior</strong></summary>
<div class="details-content">

<p>This end-to-end example shows a <strong>Head Unit ECU</strong> (intermediate node) managing a <strong>Front Camera ECU</strong> (edge node) for an ADAS feature.</p>

<h4>Step 1: YAML Parameter Schema (already defined in <code>parameters_structure.yaml</code>)</h4>
<pre><code class="yaml"># The schema says SpmTrgDvc needs:
SpmTrgDvc:
  - Name: SpmTrgDvcID         # Multiplicity: 1..Inf, Type: STRING
  - Name: SpmTrgDvcDtcBaseID  # Multiplicity: 1..1,  Type: INTEGER
  - Name: SpmTrgDvcDtcTimeOut # Multiplicity: 1..1,  Type: INTEGER
  - Name: SpmTrgDvcDiagAddr   # Multiplicity: 1..1,  Type: INTEGER</code></pre>

<h4>Step 2: Project Configuration (integrator fills in actual values)</h4>
<pre><code class="yaml"># Project-specific ECUC values (simplified):
SpmWkngDvc:
  SpmNodeType: SPM_NODE_INTERMEDIATE
  SpmSrcIp: ["192.168.1.1"]
  SpmDstIp: ["239.1.1.100"]      # Multicast

SpmTrgDvc:
  - Name: FrontCamera
    SpmTrgDvcID: ["192.168.1.50"]
    SpmTrgDvcDtcBaseID: 0x1234
    SpmTrgDvcDtcTimeOut: 3000
    SpmTrgDvcDiagAddr: 0x30
    SpmTrgDvcHndlngInfo:
      SpmTrgAssocWkUpFrm: WKUP_FRM_B
      SpmTrgAssocWkupBit: 14

SpmWkUpSeq:
  - Name: WkUpSeq_Camera
    SpmWkUpStep:
      - { SpmStepID: 1, SpmCommandType: SEND_TC10_SWTCH_1, SpmCommandValue: 3, SpmSeqStepDly: 50 }
      - { SpmStepID: 2, SpmCommandType: SEND_ETH_WKUP_FRM_A, SpmCommandValue: 5, SpmSeqStepDly: 0 }

SpmPowPrf:
  - Name: ADAS_FrontCam
    SpmSrvcAndInstID: 0x05670001
    SpmProfileIsLocal: True
    SpmLocActivationAllowed: True
    SpmApplIntfID: 42
    SpmProfBitMapIndex: 7
    SpmVehDefActPriorON: SPM_PRF_AP_HIGH
    SpmProfileSwDep:
      - SpmProfDepType: SPM_PRF_DEP_ACT_AND_CONS
        SpmProfRef: RemoteCam_Profile</code></pre>

<h4>Step 3: Generated Code (by .xpt templates)</h4>
<pre><code class="c">// Sum_Spm_Cfg.h:
#define SPM_NUM_OF_PROFILES      2
#define SPM_NUM_OF_PG_OUT_EDGE   1    // 1 target device
#define SPM_REQER_LST_SIZE       2    // targets + 1

// Sum_Spm_PBCfg.c:
const Spm_TrgDvc Spm_PowMgr_TrgDvc_List[1] = {
    [0] = {
        .ipAddr       = 0xC0A80132u,  // 192.168.1.50
        .dtcBaseId    = 0x1234u,
        .dtcTimeoutMs = 3000u,
        .diagAddr     = 0x30u,
        .wkUpFrm      = 1u,           // WKUP_FRM_B
        .wkUpBit       = 14u,
    },
};

// CDD SWCD ARXML (PGTT calibration):
// WkUpSeq_Camera: Step1={TC10, port3, 50ms}, Step2={ETH_A, bit5, 0ms}</code></pre>

<h4>Step 4: Runtime Behavior</h4>

<svg viewBox="0 0 620 370" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;max-width:620px;">
  <defs><marker id="rt_arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#003366"/></marker></defs>
