<!-- Section 10 -->
<h2 id="section-10">10. Diagnostic Services (DIDs)</h2>

<h3>DID 0xE0DD &mdash; Activation Profile Activation Status</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What</strong>: 64-byte bitmap showing which profiles are currently active</li>
  <li><strong>How</strong>: Each profile has a <code>SpmProfBitMapIndex</code> (0-511). If the profile is not INACTIVE, the corresponding bit is set to 1</li>
  <li><strong>Bit ordering</strong>: MSB first (position 0 = byte 0, bit 7)</li>
</ul>

<h3>DID 0xE0DE &mdash; Local Off-Power-Mode Activity Records</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What</strong>: Records of profiles activated by <strong>local</strong> SWCs during PowerOff sessions</li>
  <li><strong>Data per entry</strong> (7 bytes): ServiceID (2) + ProfileNumber (1) + ActivityTimer (3, seconds, big-endian) + ActivationCount (1)</li>
  <li><strong>Queue size</strong>: 5 entries, FIFO management</li>
  <li><strong>Storage</strong>: NvM block, written on <code>SUM_ARC_NvMStore</code> command</li>
</ul>

<h3>DID 0xE0DF &mdash; Remote Off-Power-Mode Activity Records</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What</strong>: Records of profiles activated by <strong>remote</strong> ECUs during PowerOff sessions</li>
  <li><strong>Data per entry</strong> (8 bytes): ServiceID (2) + ProfileNumber (1) + LastByteIPRequester (1) + ActivityTimer (3) + ActivationCount (1)</li>
  <li><strong>Queue size</strong>: 5 entries, FIFO management</li>
</ul>

<h3>DID 0xE0D7 &mdash; Activity Record via SUSD</h3>
<p>SPM communicates to SUSD via <code>SUSD_SPM_UpdateRecord</code> interface:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>RID 0x02</strong>: At least one profile is activated exclusively by a remote requester</li>
  <li><strong>RID 0x20</strong>: At least one profile has a local activation</li>
  <li><strong>RID 0x26</strong>: A wakeup frame was received with a valid wakeup bit</li>
</ul>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: DID E0DD &mdash; Building the 64-Byte Activation Bitmap</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_Diagnostic.c</code> &mdash; the bitmap is built on each DCM read request:</p>
<pre><code>#define SUM_SPM_DID_E0DD_SIZE_BYTES  64u   // 512 bits total

Std_ReturnType Runnable_SPM_DID_E0DD_ActivationProfileActivationStatus(
    Dcm_OpStatusType OpStatus, uint8* Data)
{
    // Step 1: Zero-initialize the 64-byte buffer
    for (i = 0u; i &lt; SUM_SPM_DID_E0DD_SIZE_BYTES; i++) {
        Data[i] = 0u;
    }

    // Step 2: For each configured profile, set its bit if not INACTIVE
    for (i = 0u; i &lt; SPM_CONF_POW_PRF_NUM; i++) {
        if ((SPM_PrfStsMgr_RAM[i].sm != SPM_Inactive) &amp;&amp;
            (SPM_GET_BITMAPINDEX_FROM_CONF(i) != NULL_PTR))
        {
            Spm_DID_E0DD_SetBitToOne(&amp;Data[0u], *(SPM_GET_BITMAPINDEX_FROM_CONF(i)));
        }
    }
    return E_OK;
}

// MSB-first bit positioning (position 0 = byte 0, bit 7)
static void Spm_DID_E0DD_SetBitToOne(uint8* Data, const uint16 position) {
    if (position &lt; 512u) {
        uint8 bytePosition = (uint8)(position / 8u);
        uint8 bitPosition  = (uint8)(7u - (position % 8u));  // MSB-first!
        Data[bytePosition] |= 1u &lt;&lt; bitPosition;
    }
}

// Example: Profile with SpmProfBitMapIndex = 5
//   bytePosition = 5 / 8 = 0
//   bitPosition  = 7 - (5 % 8) = 7 - 5 = 2
//   Data[0] |= (1 &lt;&lt; 2) = 0x04
//   So bit 5 maps to byte 0, bit 2 (MSB-first ordering)</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: DID E0DE/E0DF &mdash; Activity Record Serialization</h4>
  <p>Each DID record contains activation history for off-power-mode sessions:</p>
<pre><code>// DID E0DE (Local) - 7 bytes per record, 5 records max = 35 bytes total
// Layout per record:
//   [ServiceID_Hi][ServiceID_Lo][ProfileNumber][Timer_Hi][Timer_Mid][Timer_Lo][ActivationCount]

// DID E0DF (Remote) - 8 bytes per record, 5 records max = 40 bytes total
// Layout per record:
//   [ServiceID_Hi][ServiceID_Lo][ProfileNumber][LastByteIP][Timer_Hi][Timer_Mid][Timer_Lo][ActivationCount]

// ActivityTimer conversion: internal ticks &rarr; seconds (big-endian, 3 bytes)
// Timer is incremented each SM main cycle while the profile is active
// On serialization: ticks * SUM_SPM_PERIOD_SM_MAINFUNCTION_MS / 1000 = seconds

// The records are managed as a FIFO (deque):
//   - New activation: if record exists for this profile, increment count + reset timer
//   - If full: PopFront (discard oldest), PushBack (new record)
//   - NvM persistence: written on SUM_ARC_NvMStore command

// Tick-to-seconds conversion during serialization:
actvTimer_seconds = (ActivityTimerInTick * SPM_SM_PERIODICITY_MS) / 1000U;
// SPM_SM_PERIODICITY_MS = 10ms, so 100 ticks = 1 second

// Stored as big-endian 3 bytes:
Data[pos]     = (uint8)(actvTimer_seconds &gt;&gt; 16U);   // MSB
Data[pos + 1] = (uint8)(actvTimer_seconds &gt;&gt; 8U);
Data[pos + 2] = (uint8)(actvTimer_seconds &amp; 0xFF);   // LSB</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Code Example: ActivityRecordCmd &mdash; SUSD Control Interface</h4>
  <p>From <code>Sum_Spm_Diagnostic.c</code> &mdash; SUSD controls DID recording via commands:</p>
<pre><code>uint8 SUM_SPM_DID_E0DE_Data[35] = {0u};   // RAM mirror for NvM (5 local x 7 bytes)
uint8 SUM_SPM_DID_E0DF_Data[40] = {0u};   // RAM mirror for NvM (5 remote x 8 bytes)

SPM_ActivityRecordCmd(SPM_SUSD_ActivityRecordCmdType Cmd) {
    switch (Cmd) {
        case SUM_ARC_Reset:
            Spm_ClearQueueDID_E0DE_E0DF();     // clear both deques
            // NOTE: intentional fall-through to NvMStore!

        case SUM_ARC_NvMStore:
            // Serialize current queues into RAM buffers
            Runnable_Spm_DID0xE0DE(DCM_INITIAL, &amp;SUM_SPM_DID_E0DE_Data[0]);
            Runnable_Spm_DID0xE0DF(DCM_INITIAL, &amp;SUM_SPM_DID_E0DF_Data[0]);
            // Persist to NvM
            Rte_Call_RP_SPM_Dcm_E0DE_Write_WriteBlock(&amp;SUM_SPM_DID_E0DE_Data[0]);
            Rte_Call_RP_SPM_Dcm_E0DF_Write_WriteBlock(&amp;SUM_SPM_DID_E0DF_Data[0]);
            break;

        case SUM_ARC_UpdateRecord:
            Spm_E0D7ActiveStatus = E0D7_ACTIVE;      // enable recording
            break;

        case SUM_ARC_StopUpdate:
            Spm_E0D7ActiveStatus = E0D7_NOT_ACTIVE;   // disable recording
            break;
    }
}</code></pre>
  <blockquote><p><strong>Key insight:</strong> <code>SUM_ARC_Reset</code> intentionally falls through to <code>SUM_ARC_NvMStore</code> &mdash; clearing the queues AND immediately persisting the empty state to NvM in a single command. This prevents stale data from surviving a power cycle.</p></blockquote>
</div>

<hr>

