<h3>Typical Development Cycle</h3>

<pre><code>1. Understand requirement (SRS -&gt; DDS traceability)
2. Edit template (.xpt) or config (.arxml/.yaml)
3. Run code generation (step 04)
4. Run static analysis (step 08) -- fix MISRA violations
5. Update/create unit tests
6. Run tests (step 09) -- ensure MC/DC coverage
7. Update traceability (step 10)
8. Create PR with evidence (MISRA report, test report, traceability)</code></pre>

<h3>Git Conventions</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Branches</strong>: <code>feature/GMSUM-XXXX-description</code> or <code>bugfix/GMSUM-XXXX-description</code></li>
  <li><strong>Commits</strong>: <code>GMSUM-XXXX: Description</code></li>
  <li><strong>PR target</strong>: Release branch (e.g., <code>release/8.1.0</code>)</li>
  <li><strong>PR must include</strong>: MISRA report, test report, traceability report as evidence</li>
</ul>

