<h2 id="paramdef">13. Parameter Definition (ECUC ParamDef)</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom:1rem;color:#64748b;font-size:.92rem;">Interactive ECUC parameter definition tree for <strong>SPM</strong>. Click on containers (&#9654;) to expand and view parameters, types, ranges, defaults, and references.</p>
<div class="module-desc-box">
      <strong>SPM</strong> manages power profiles, target device wake-up sequences, and network VLAN communications.
      It has the most complex ParamDef with 14 containers covering general settings, power profiles, profile dependencies, target/waking devices, and wake-up sequences.
    </div>

    <div class="pd-tree">
      <div class="pd-node">
        <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
          <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span>
          <span class="pd-icon root">M</span>
          <span class="pd-name">Spm</span>
          <span class="pd-mult">0..1</span>
          <span class="pd-brief">&mdash; Software/Power Manager (45 params, 30 refs, 16 containers)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-children hidden">

          <!-- SpmGeneral -->
          <div class="pd-node">
            <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
              <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span>
              <span class="pd-icon container">C</span>
              <span class="pd-name">SpmGeneral</span>
              <span class="pd-mult">1..1</span>
              <span class="pd-count">14 params</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pd-body">
              <div class="pd-desc">General SPM timing, execution, queue sizing, and calibration parameters.</div>
              <div class="pd-section-title">Parameters</div>
              <div class="pd-hdr param-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Range</span><span>Default</span><span>Description</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmSMMainFuncPeriodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">Min: 5.0</span><span class="pdef">10.0</span><span class="pdesc">Software Manager main function periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmPMMainFuncPeriodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">Min: 5.0</span><span class="pdef">5.0</span><span class="pdesc">Power Manager main function periodicity in ms (currently fixed to 5ms).</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmBurstPhsPeriodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">Min: 5</span><span class="pdef">5</span><span class="pdesc">Burst phase message periodicity in ms (first 3 counts).</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmPermitExecutionMask</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;255</span><span class="pdef">254</span><span class="pdesc">Bitmap defining wakeup sources for SPM execution.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmWkUpHelperFunction</span><span class="type-badge type-str">STRING</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Custom wake-up helper function name. For intermediate nodes only.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmGenerateInitRunnable</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">False</span><span class="pdesc">If TRUE, generates SPM init runnable. Otherwise called by BswM.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmInitFuncPeriodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">1.0&ndash;5000.0</span><span class="pdef">1000.0</span><span class="pdesc">Init runnable periodicity in ms. Required when SpmGenerateInitRunnable = TRUE.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">Spm_SmFrame_QueueLength</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Max queue length of SM Frame Rx messages.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">Spm_PmHeartbeat_QueueLength</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Max queue length of PM heartbeat Rx messages.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">Spm_PmETHwakeUpUNIC_QueueLength</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Max queue length of PM ETH wakeup Unicast Rx messages.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">Spm_PmETHwakeUpMULTIC_QueueLength</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Max queue length of PM ETH wakeup Multicast Rx messages.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">Spm_LocalRequests_QueueLength</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Max queue length of local activation/deactivation + diagnostic requests.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmHBShutdownDelayMs</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65000</span><span class="pdef">2000</span><span class="pdesc">Time in ms PM waits after last burst HeartBeat before allowing shutdown.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmSMStayAwakeTimeMs</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65000</span><span class="pdef">2000</span><span class="pdesc">Time in ms SM stays awake if only requester is in fault/restart state.</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="pd-children hidden">
              <div class="pd-node">
                <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
                  <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span>
                  <span class="pd-icon sub">S</span>
                  <span class="pd-name">SpmDiagnostic</span>
                  <span class="pd-mult">0..1</span>
                  <span class="pd-count">5 refs</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pd-body">
                  <div class="pd-desc">DCM DID and NvM references for SPM diagnostic data.</div>
                  <div class="pd-section-title">References</div>
                  <div class="pd-hdr ref-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Target</span><span>Description</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-ref"><span class="pn">spm_DID_E0DD_...DCM_Ref</span><span class="type-badge type-ref">REF</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">Dcm &rarr; DcmDspDid</span><span class="pdesc">DID 0xE0DD Activation Profile Activation Status.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-ref"><span class="pn">SpmDID0xE0DEDcmRef</span><span class="type-badge type-ref">REF</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">Dcm &rarr; DcmDspDid</span><span class="pdesc">DID 0xE0DE Local Activated Profile Off Power Mode Records.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-ref"><span class="pn">SpmDID0xE0DFDcmRef</span><span class="type-badge type-ref">REF</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">Dcm &rarr; DcmDspDid</span><span class="pdesc">DID 0xE0DF Remote Activated Profile Off Power Mode Records.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-ref"><span class="pn">SpmDID0xE0DENvmRef</span><span class="type-badge type-ref">REF</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">NvM &rarr; NvMBlockDescriptor</span><span class="pdesc">NvM block for DID 0xE0DE local activation records.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-ref"><span class="pn">SpmDID0xE0DFNvmRef</span><span class="type-badge type-ref">REF</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">NvM &rarr; NvMBlockDescriptor</span><span class="pdesc">NvM block for DID 0xE0DF remote activation records.</span></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pd-node">
                <div class="pd-header leaf"><span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmCANWkUpFrmRef</span><span class="pd-mult">0..1</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; CAN wake-up frame references</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="pd-node">
                <div class="pd-header leaf"><span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmVLANCom</span><span class="pd-mult">1..*</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; per-VLAN communication (Heartbeat, WakeupFrames, SwrMgrInfo)</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- SpmConfigSet -->
          <div class="pd-node">
            <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
              <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span>
              <span class="pd-icon container">C</span>
              <span class="pd-name">SpmConfigSet</span>
              <span class="pd-mult">1..1</span>
              <span class="pd-brief">&mdash; power profiles, power graph, target devices</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pd-children hidden">
              <div class="pd-node">
                <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
                  <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span>
                  <span class="pd-icon sub">S</span>
                  <span class="pd-name">SpmPowPrf</span>
                  <span class="pd-mult">1..*</span>
                  <span class="pd-count">10 params</span>
                  <span class="pd-brief">&mdash; power profiles</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pd-body">
                  <div class="pd-desc">Core SPM container defining each power profile with service IDs, priorities, activation rules, and COM PDU group references.</div>
                  <div class="pd-section-title">Parameters</div>
                  <div class="pd-hdr param-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Range</span><span>Default</span><span>Description</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmSrvcAndInstID</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">Max: 4294967291</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Service and Instance ID for the profile.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmProfNumber</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;255</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Profile number.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmProfileIsLocal</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">False</span><span class="pdesc">Whether this profile is local to the ECU.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmLocActivationAllowed</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">False</span><span class="pdesc">Whether local activation is allowed.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmProfBitMapIndex</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;511</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Bitmap index for profile status reported by DID E0DD.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmApplIntfID</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Application interface ID for the profile.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmProfActivationTimeOutVehOff</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Activation timeout when vehicle is OFF.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmVehDefActPriorON</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">NOTAPP..ACCESS</span><span class="pdef">SPM_PRF_AP_NOTAPP</span><span class="pdesc">Default activation priority when vehicle is ON.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmVehDefActPriorOFF</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">NOTAPP..EMERGENCY</span><span class="pdef">SPM_PRF_AP_NOTAPP</span><span class="pdesc">Default activation priority when vehicle is OFF.</span></div>
                  <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmComIPduGroupEvnt_Tx/Rx</span><span class="type-badge type-ref">REF</span><span class="pm">0..*</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">References to COM IPdu group events for Tx and Rx.</span></div>
                </div>
                <div class="pd-children hidden">
                  <div class="pd-node"><div class="pd-header leaf"><span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmProfileSwDep</span><span class="pd-mult">0..*</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; profile software dependencies</span></div></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pd-node">
                <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
                  <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span>
                  <span class="pd-icon sub">S</span>
                  <span class="pd-name">SpmPgttEntries</span>
                  <span class="pd-mult">1..1</span>
                  <span class="pd-brief">&mdash; Power Graph / network topology</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pd-children hidden">
                  <div class="pd-node">
                    <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
                      <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmTrgDvc</span><span class="pd-mult">1..*</span><span class="pd-count">6 params</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pd-body">
                      <div class="pd-desc">Defines target devices that SPM can wake up, with DTC reporting and diagnostic addressing.</div>
                      <div class="pd-section-title">Parameters</div>
                      <div class="pd-hdr param-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Range</span><span>Default</span><span>Description</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmTrgDvcID</span><span class="type-badge type-str">STRING</span><span class="pm">1..*</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Target device identifier(s).</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmTrgDvcDtcBaseID</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">DTC base ID for this target device.</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmTrgDvcDtcTimeOut</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">DTC timeout for this target device.</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmTrgDvcDiagAddr</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;255</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Diagnostic address for diagnostic sessions.</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmTrgDvcPowerOnDeviceRetryPeriodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">10000</span><span class="pdesc">Periodicity in ms of PowerOnDevice retry.</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmTrgDvcPowerOnDevice...OffandOnSequence</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">1000</span><span class="pdesc">Wait time in ms between OFF and ON sequence during retry (&gt;250ms).</span></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pd-children hidden">
                      <div class="pd-node"><div class="pd-header leaf"><span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmTrgDvcVariantHndlng</span><span class="pd-mult">0..*</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; per-variant wakeup config</span></div></div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="pd-node"><div class="pd-header leaf"><span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmWkngDvc</span><span class="pd-mult">1..1</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; local node type (EDGE/INTERMEDIATE)</span></div></div>
                  <div class="pd-node">
                    <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
                      <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmVariantCfg</span><span class="pd-mult">1..*</span><span class="pd-count">3 params</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pd-body">
                      <div class="pd-desc">Hardware variant configuration. Defines wakeup frame/bit, intermediate node addresses, and per-VLAN heartbeat IPs.</div>
                      <div class="pd-section-title">Parameters</div>
                      <div class="pd-hdr param-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Range</span><span>Default</span><span>Description</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmVariantWkupFrame</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">WKUP_FRM_A/B/C</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Wake-up frame for this variant.</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmVariantWkupBit</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;63</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Wake-up bit position for this variant.</span></div>
                      <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmVariantIntermediateDstAddr</span><span class="type-badge type-str">STRING</span><span class="pm">0..*</span><span class="pr">IPv4</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">IP addresses of intermediate nodes for this variant.</span></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pd-children hidden">
                      <div class="pd-node"><div class="pd-header leaf"><span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmVariantHBVLANCfg</span><span class="pd-mult">1..*</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; per-VLAN heartbeat IPs</span></div></div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="pd-node">
                    <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
                      <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmWkUpSeq</span><span class="pd-mult">0..*</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; wake-up sequences</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pd-children hidden">
                      <div class="pd-node">
                        <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
                          <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmWkUpStep</span><span class="pd-mult">1..*</span><span class="pd-count">4 params</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="pd-body">
                          <div class="pd-desc">Individual steps in a wake-up sequence, specifying command type, value, and delay.</div>
                          <div class="pd-section-title">Parameters</div>
                          <div class="pd-hdr param-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Range</span><span>Default</span><span>Description</span></div>
                          <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmStepID</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">1&ndash;255</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Step identifier in the sequence.</span></div>
                          <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmCommandType</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">TC10_SWTCH, ETH/CAN_WKUP, LV_GPIO</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Type of wake-up command to send.</span></div>
                          <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmCommandValue</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;255</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Value associated with the command.</span></div>
                          <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SpmSeqStepDly</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Delay in ms before executing this step.</span></div>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pd-node"><div class="pd-header leaf"><span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon sub">S</span><span class="pd-name">SpmLowVoltagePowerInfo</span><span class="pd-mult">0..1</span><span class="pd-brief">&mdash; LV Energy Optimizer integration</span></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="explain-box">
      <div class="title">How SPM ParamDef    <div class="explain-box">
      <div class="title">How SPM ParamDef works with the module</div>
      SPM is the most configuration-heavy SUM module (45 params, 30 refs, 16 containers).
      <br><br>
      <strong>SpmConfigSet</strong> contains the three core subsystems:<br>
      1. <strong>Power Profiles (SpmPowPrf)</strong> - define services/features needing power, their activation priorities (NOTAPP through EMERGENCY), and COM IPdu group references for enabling/disabling network Tx/Rx per profile. Profiles can have software dependencies (SpmProfileSwDep).<br>
      2. <strong>Power Graph (SpmPgttEntries)</strong> - the network topology: target devices (with IPv4 addresses, DTC reporting), waking device config (EDGE vs INTERMEDIATE node), HW variants (SpmVariantCfg with per-VLAN heartbeat IPs), and wake-up sequences.<br>
      3. <strong>LowVoltagePowerInfo</strong> - optional LV Energy Optimizer integration.<br><br>
      <strong>SpmGeneral</strong> provides timing (SM/PM periodicities), queue sizes for Rx message buffering, calibration timers (HeartBeat shutdown delay, SM stay-awake time), and sub-containers for diagnostics (DID E0DD/E0DE/E0DF), CAN wake-up frame references, and VLAN communication interfaces (heartbeat, wakeup frames, SW manager info - each with Tx/Rx FOREIGN-REFs to IMPLEMENTATION-DATA-TYPE and SENDER-RECEIVER-INTERFACE).
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ==================== LNM ==================== -->
<section id="mod-lnm" class="module-section">
<div class="module-card">
  <div class="module-header" onclick="toggleModule(this)">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px">
      <span class="badge">LNM</span>
      <h2>LIN Network Manager</h2>
    </div>
    <span class="arrow">&#9654;</span>
  </div>
  <div class="module-body">
    <div class="module-desc-box">
      <strong>LNM</strong> manages the local network schedule states and transitions.
      It implements a configurable state machine for network scheduling with arbitration logic based on inputs, conditions, and rules.
      The ParamDef defines a rich hierarchy of containers for building project-specific network management logic.
    </div>

    <div class="pd-tree">
      <div class="pd-node">
        <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
          <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon root">M</span><span class="pd-name">LNM</span><span class="pd-mult">0..1</span>
          <span class="pd-brief">&mdash; LIN Network Manager</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-children hidden">

          <!-- LNM_General -->
          <div class="pd-node">
            <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
              <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon container">C</span><span class="pd-name">LNM_General</span><span class="pd-mult">1..1</span><span class="pd-count">15 params</span><span class="pd-count">1 ref</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pd-body">
              <div class="pd-desc">General configuration parameters of SUM_LNM - periodicities, execution mask, wakeup delays, CyberFill, and initialization settings.</div>
              <div class="pd-section-title">Parameters</div>
              <div class="pd-hdr param-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Range</span><span>Default</span><span>Description</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_MainFunction_Period</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0.001&ndash;0.2</span><span class="pdef">0.1</span><span class="pdesc">Time in sec for the periodicity of the MainFunction runnable.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_NetworkStatus_Period</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0.001&ndash;0.2</span><span class="pdef">0.1</span><span class="pdesc">Time in sec for the periodicity of NetworkStatus.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_ScheduleManagement_Period</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0.001&ndash;0.2</span><span class="pdef">0.1</span><span class="pdesc">Time in sec for the periodicity of ScheduleManagement.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_NetworkFaultManager_Period</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0.001&ndash;0.2</span><span class="pdef">0.1</span><span class="pdesc">Time in sec for the periodicity of NetworkFaultManager.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_PermitExecution_Mask</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">254</span><span class="pdesc">Mask checked by SUM_LNM to execute its functions.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_TWuDelay_Commander</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;200</span><span class="pdef">100</span><span class="pdesc">Delay in ms before schedule activation when wakeup requested by Commander.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_TWuDelay_Responder</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;200</span><span class="pdef">100</span><span class="pdesc">Delay in ms before schedule activation when wakeup requested by Responder.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_WupTxRetries_Commander</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;255</span><span class="pdef">10</span><span class="pdesc">Retries before Loss of Communication notification.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">CyberFill_Supported</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">false</span><span class="pdesc">Enable CyberFill value support.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LNM_CyberFillValue</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">CyberFill value provided by SUM_LNM at initialization.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LnmGenerateInitRunnable</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">false</span><span class="pdesc">If TRUE, generates periodic runnable for init().</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">LnmInitFuncPeriodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">1.0&ndash;5000.0</span><span class="pdef">1000.0</span><span class="pdesc">Periodicity in ms of RE_Lnm_Init.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">Sum_Lnm_ConfGen_Enabled</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">false</span><span class="pdesc">If true, ConfGen generates Sum_Lnm_SWCD.arxml.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">Sum_Lnm_ScheduleChannelUserFuncs_Enabled</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">false</span><span class="pdesc">Enable user functions for changing Schedule Table and Channel State.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">lNM_C_DTC_LostCommWithLinResp_Enabled</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">true</span><span class="pdesc">Calibration parameter to enable/disable Lost Communication with LIN Responder DTC.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-section-title">References</div>
