    </div>

    <div class="explain-box">
      <div class="title">How SSFM ParamDef    <div class="explain-box">
      <div class="title">How SSFM ParamDef works with the module</div>
      SSFM's ParamDef mirrors its complex dual sub-module architecture:
      <ul style="margin:8px 0 4px 18px">
        <li><strong>SSM side</strong>: <em>Sum_Ssfm_SerialData</em> instances define every CAN/Ethernet signal the module monitors. Each links to an <em>RteSerialData</em> callback, a <em>Channel</em>, optional SecOC/PN/SD references, and FcI/FoI/FpI/FsI debouncers. <em>GroupInfo</em> organizes these by ECU, LIN responder, or target device with per-group DEM event mappings and debounce timers.</li>
        <li><strong>ERRH side</strong>: <em>ErrorsHandlers</em> categorizes errors by source (BSW, LNM, SUSD, SSC, SrvcMgr, Safety/Security) with individual DTC process flags. <em>ErrorFilter</em> provides reusable filtering methods (X_OF_Y windowing or BLOCK) that any error handler can reference.</li>
        <li><strong>DID/NvM</strong>: <em>Errh_DID</em> configures diagnostic DIDs (E0B8&ndash;E0BB, F094) and their NvM block storage for persistent error data across power cycles.</li>
      </ul>
      The two separate PermitExecutionMasks (SSM vs ERRH) allow SUSD to independently control startup of each sub-module based on wakeup source.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ==================== SUSD ==================== -->
<section id="mod-susd" class="module-section">
<div class="module-card">
  <div class="module-header" onclick="toggleModule(this)">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px">
      <span class="badge">SUSD</span>
      <h2>Start Up / Shut Down Coordinator</h2>
    </div>
    <span class="arrow">&#9654;</span>
  </div>
  <div class="module-body">
    <div class="module-desc-box">
      <strong>SUSD</strong> is the startup orchestrator for all SUM modules. It manages wakeup source identification, Permit Execution distribution, and SUM interface initialization.
      It determines which wakeup event triggered the ECU start and distributes execution permissions to other SUM modules via PermitExecutionMask.
    </div>

    <div class="pd-tree">
      <div class="pd-node">
        <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
          <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon root">M</span><span class="pd-name">SUSD</span><span class="pd-mult">0..1</span>
          <span class="pd-brief">&mdash; Start Up / Shut Down Coordinator (51 params, 24 refs, 9 containers)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pd-children hidden">

          <!-- SUSDGeneral -->
          <div class="pd-node">
            <div class="pd-header" onclick="toggleTree(this)">
              <span class="pd-toggle">&#9654;</span><span class="pd-icon container">C</span><span class="pd-name">SUSDGeneral</span><span class="pd-mult">1..1</span><span class="pd-count">23 params</span><span class="pd-count">7 refs</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pd-body">
              <div class="pd-desc">General SUSD configuration: timing periodicities, VPM determination, RunCrank settings, feature flags, and diagnostic DID references.</div>
              <div class="pd-section-title">Parameters</div>
              <div class="pd-hdr param-hdr"><span>Name</span><span>Type</span><span>Mult</span><span>Range</span><span>Default</span><span>Description</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_Shutdown_Refresh</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0.001&ndash;0.5</span><span class="pdef">0.1</span><span class="pdesc">ShutdownPermission signal refresh time in sec.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_Force_Shutdown_Wait</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65.535</span><span class="pdef">0</span><span class="pdesc">Wait time before requesting Shutdown from BswM.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_Battery_Periodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">1&ndash;500</span><span class="pdef">100</span><span class="pdesc">Battery Monitor notification periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_VehiclePowerMode_Periodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">1&ndash;500</span><span class="pdef">100</span><span class="pdesc">Vehicle Power Mode notification periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_ResetExecution_Periodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">1.0&ndash;65.535</span><span class="pdef">1.0</span><span class="pdesc">Reset Execution timer periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_RunCrank_Periodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">1&ndash;500</span><span class="pdef">100</span><span class="pdesc">Run Crank notification periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_Wakeup_Periodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">1&ndash;500</span><span class="pdef">100</span><span class="pdesc">Wakeup polling periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_t_AppManager_Periodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">1&ndash;500</span><span class="pdef">100</span><span class="pdesc">AppStateManager periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SusdGenerateInitRunnable</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">False</span><span class="pdesc">If TRUE, generates SUSD init runnable.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SusdInitFuncPeriodicity</span><span class="type-badge type-float">FLOAT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">1.0&ndash;5000.0</span><span class="pdef">1000.0</span><span class="pdesc">Init runnable periodicity in ms.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_PowerModing_Slave_Supported</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">false</span><span class="pdesc">True if ECU is not the Power Mode Master.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_RunCrankPlausibility_Supported</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">false</span><span class="pdesc">True if RunCrank Input available from SWC.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_C_DefaultShutdownState</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">Off, Sleep</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Default ECU operation state when shutting down.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_VPM_SPM_Initial</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">SUM_PMS_OFF..TRANSPORT</span><span class="pdef">SUM_PMS_OFF</span><span class="pdesc">Initial System Power Mode for VPM.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_VPM_SBPM_Initial</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">SUM_PMS_OFF..TRANSPORT</span><span class="pdef">SUM_PMS_OFF</span><span class="pdesc">Initial Backup Power Mode for VPM.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_VPM_Security_Supported</span><span class="type-badge type-enum">ENUM</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">NOT_Applicable, With_OBD, etc.</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">VPM determination with/without Cybersecurity.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_PermitExecAvailable</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">true</span><span class="pdesc">Permit Execution Interface for this SWC.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUM_SUSD_RESETExecution_TIMER_Thresh_Init</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;10</span><span class="pdef">10</span><span class="pdesc">Reset execution timer threshold init value.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_C_RunningResetWaitTime</span><span class="type-badge type-int">INT</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">0&ndash;65535</span><span class="pdef">625</span><span class="pdesc">Wait time before running reset.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_Battery_State_of_Charge_Supported</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">false</span><span class="pdesc">Enable Battery State of Charge support.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_VPM_ASIL_A_Supported</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">&mdash;</span><span class="pdesc">Enable ASIL-A support for VPM.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_DisNvMWriteAvailable</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">0..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">true</span><span class="pdesc">Enable Disable NvM Write interface.</span></div>
              <div class="pd-param"><span class="pn">SUSD_ECUOpStateDIDSupported</span><span class="type-badge type-bool">BOOL</span><span class="pm">1..1</span><span class="pr">&mdash;</span><span class="pdef">true</span><span class="pdesc">Enable ECU Operation State DID support.</span></div>
